  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming React Compatibility**\n\nI\'ve confirmed React 19 (`^19.0.1`) is installed. This is crucial because `@react-three/fiber` v9 supports it, and `@react-three/drei` v10 requires `@react-three/fiber` v9, and is also compatible. I\'m also ensuring the correct versions of `three` and `@types/three` are in use.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Performance & Style**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing performance and visual style. I\'ve decided against `@react-three/postprocessing` due to React 19 compatibility concerns. I\'m focusing on Three.js PBR, custom GLSL shaders, `ACESFilmicToneMapping`, and `RoomEnvironment` for stunning visuals without performance bottlenecks. The necessary packages, `[\"three\", \"@types/three\", \"@react-three/fiber\", \"@react-three/drei\"]`, will be installed next via a single call, and I will be updating `/metadata.json` and `/index.html` in parallel.\n\n\n**Defining Applet Architecture**\n\nI\'m now deep in the design phase for the modular architecture of the project. I\'m focusing on creating clean, focused, and well-typed files to avoid any GC issues in the render loop. I\'m prioritizing future-proofing the project for phases 2-5, considering multiple ship types, combat mechanics, and a mission structure. The primary files I am concentrating on now are `src/types/game.ts` and `src/components/ThreeCanvas.tsx`.\n\n\n**Constructing Ship Configurations**\n\nI\'m now building the `src/config/ships.ts` registry. It will hold configurations for all three playable fighters. This includes detailed specifications for the Interceptor (Phase 1), Striker (Phase 2 unlock), and Destroyer. The Interceptor\'s model is complete. I\'m focusing on creating distinct procedural 3D geometry profiles for all three ships. This is to make the hangar truly impressive, and clearly indicate Striker and Destroyer\'s \"Phase 2\" status within the hangar.\n\n\n**Implementing Phase 1 Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core features for Phase 1. The flight prototype will be launched first, and I will then build out the ship selection system. The hangar will display the ship selection system in a preview state, and the settings menu will support mouse sensitivity and audio volume adjustments. I am ensuring that all non-functional buttons are clearly marked as \"Coming Soon.\" I will prioritize building full 3D geometry builders for the Interceptor, and also 3D preview silhouettes for Striker & Destroyer in the Hangar to make it interactive and visually engaging.\n\n\n**Building Asset Pipelines**\n\nI\'m now building an asset manager with caching and reference counting. I\'m focusing on procedural texture generators for brushed metallic hull panel maps. I\'m leveraging offscreen Canvas2D with `SRGBColorSpace` and anisotropy. I\'ll also build procedural planet surface and ring textures, and soft radial glow sprite textures. I\'ll also add lazy loading stages with real progress callbacks (`onProgress(stage, percent)`) and safe disposal. I\'ve also constructed `src/engine/InputManager.ts`, a clean, decoupled keyboard + Pointer Lock mouse manager. It handles key events and mouse deltas, with Pointer Lock fallback and clear HUD prompts.\n\n\n**Expanding Flight Controls**\n\nI\'m now expanding the flight controls to support both Pointer Lock and arrow key navigation. This includes a 6DOF arcade space flight simulation within `src/engine/FlightController.ts`. I\'m using TypeScript, with zero React dependency and pre-allocated scratch objects for performance, with the ship forward set to -Z. The inputs will be mouse X for yaw, mouse Y for pitch, and A/D for independent roll. Arrow keys will now be supported as optional fallbacks.\n\n\n**Defining Flight Physics**\n\nI\'m now defining the flight physics for the Interceptor. I\'m focusing on arcade-style 6DOF flight with WASD and shift for thrust and boost. Boost will be energy-based with a drain and regen cycle, while inertia will smoothly align with the ship\'s facing direction. I\'ll need to write live telemetry, which I\'ll be implementing immediately, including speed, throttle, and more, as well as ensure the smooth damping of all flight dynamics.\n\n\n**Constructing Chase Camera**\n\nI\'m now building `src/engine/CameraController.ts`, a pure TypeScript third-person chase camera controller. It\'ll track the player ship smoothly and at configurable distances. I\'m implementing damped positional and rotational tracking for a cinematic feel. It will feature a dynamic FOV with subtle micro-vibrations during boost, with support for menu and hangar orbit cameras.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Soundscape**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dynamic soundscape. I\'ve focused on synthesizing engine hum, boost afterburner, and UI interactions with engine sounds that change based on ship speed and throttle. I\'m also ensuring the soundscape is properly muted in the menu or when paused. I\'ve designed a clear sound system with an unmount cleanup.\n\n**Refining Hangar & Scene**\n\nI\'m working on the Hangar previews and the space sector scene now. I\'m extracting `\'interceptor\'`, `\'striker\'`, and `\'destroyer\'` models from `ShipConfig` so all three hulls can be previewed. I\'m also creating a cinematic 3D space sector, complete with a custom GLSL deep-space nebula skybox shader and a multi-layer instanced starfield with color variation and a twinkle shader. I will also be creating an `updateVisuals` handle to control engine glow, plume effects, and control surface visuals.\n\n\n**Designing Scene Assets**\n\nI\'m now designing the crucial scene assets to enrich the Hangar and in-flight experience. I\'m focusing on distant cinematic planets like Aurelia Prime and its scarred moon, with procedural textures and atmospheric effects. I\'m also planning an asteroid belt and relay beacons to establish scale and spatial reference. Three-point lighting will be combined with `RoomEnvironment` PMREM for optimal visual quality. I\'ll add all of these assets to the existing scene.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Effects**\n\nI\'m now implementing visual effects. I\'m building `src/scene/SpeedLinesVFX.tsx` for zero-allocation instanced space-dust streaks and boost warp speed-lines. These will surround the ship\'s flight corridor. I\'m ensuring continuous particle wrapping around the ship\'s world position.\n\nI am also refining the overall scene setup by updating `src/scene/GameScene.tsx` and `src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx` to utilize React Three Fiber `<Canvas>` for isolating full-viewport rendering. This includes implementing `ACESFilmicToneMapping` and `SRGBColorSpace`. I\'ll run `FlightController`, `CameraController`, ship visual updates, and `AudioManager.updateFlightAudio(...)` within the R3F `useFrame` hook, with zero React state updates per frame. I will also incorporate a non-intrusive performance monitor for tracking and analysis.\n\n\n**Constructing In-Flight HUD**\n\nI\'m currently building the in-flight HUD, focusing on a minimalist, tactical design. I\'m leveraging `Oxanium` and `JetBrains Mono` fonts with electric cyan on translucent dark navy scrims for visual clarity. The HUD will be updated via a DOM-ref loop reading directly from a mutable `FlightTelemetry` ref for optimal performance. The planned elements are a precision aiming reticle, hull integrity and ship designation, a boost energy gauge with flight status, and a velocity readout with throttle bar.\n\n\n**Designing Main Menu**\n\nI\'m now designing the main menu UI and its cinematic overlay. I\'m focusing on a clean aesthetic with a \"STARFALL\" typographic wordmark and a focused action column. The menu will feature \"Play,\" \"Hangar,\" and \"Settings\" options. The settings menu will include mouse sensitivity, camera distance, and volume controls.\n\n\n"
