  planner_response {
    response: "**STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 1: Project Foundation & Flight Prototype** has been implemented and verified.\n\n### 1. Summary of Implemented Features\n- **3D Space Environment**: Deep-space procedural GLSL nebula skybox anchored to camera coordinates, multi-spectral twinkling starfield, ringed gas giant (*Aurelia Prime*) with Fresnel atmospheric rim glow and procedural ring banding, cratered rocky moon, instanced asteroid belt, orbital navigation beacons, and a 3-point lighting rig paired with `RoomEnvironment` PMREM reflections.\n- **Player Spaceship & Hangar Chassis**: Multi-part procedural 3D PBR space fighters (`THREE.Group` with beveled wings, sculpted fuselage, armored cockpit canopy, wing cannon pods, and custom GLSL volumetric plasma exhaust plumes). The **VX-9 Vanguard (Interceptor)** is active for flight; **SR-4 Valkyrie (Striker)** and **HX-12 Aegis (Destroyer)** are inspectable in 3D in the Hangar and marked as coming soon.\n- **6DOF Arcade Flight Controller**: Quaternion-based local-space pitch, yaw, and independent roll (`A`/`D`), relative mouse steering via Pointer Lock API (with drag-to-steer and arrow-key fallbacks), forward/reverse thrust (`W`/`S`), arcade lateral velocity alignment with controlled inertia, and configurable sensitivity / invert-Y.\n- **Boost System**: Holding `Shift` multiplies speed and acceleration, intensifies engine glow and exhaust length, widens chase camera FOV, activates instanced space-dust/boost speed lines, drains boost energy, enforces a short lockout on full depletion, and regenerates energy after a cooldown.\n- **Third-Person Chase Camera**: Frame-rate-independent exponentially damped follow position and quaternion tracking, subtle turn lead/lag clamped so the fighter stays framed, dynamic boost FOV widening (`62\302\260` \342\206\222 `~78.5\302\260`), subtle boost micro-vibration, and smooth Menu/Hangar showcase orbits.\n- **Zero-Re-Render Flight HUD**: Updates velocity, hull integrity, boost energy, flight status, heading/pitch/roll readout, dynamic turn-lead reticle, and optional performance telemetry (`FPS`, frame time, draw calls, triangle count) via a `requestAnimationFrame` DOM-ref loop without per-frame React state updates. Includes collapsible control hints (`H`) and click-to-lock prompt.\n- **Menu, Hangar, Pause & Settings**: Live-3D Main Menu (`Play`, `Hangar`, `Settings`), interactive drag-to-orbit 3D Hangar with comparative ship specs, progressive Loading screen, `Esc` pause overlay (`Resume Flight`, `Settings`, `Reset Flight Position`, `Main Menu`), and locally persisted Settings (mouse sensitivity, invert pitch, camera distance, tracking responsiveness, master volume, graphics quality presets, performance overlay).\n- **Procedural Web Audio Engine**: Synthesized ion engine hum (pitch/filter tracked to velocity and throttle), afterburner boost roar + engage burst, and UI hover/click/pause sounds unlocked on user gesture with master volume control.\n\n### 2. Project Architecture\n- **Engine & Simulation (`src/engine/`)**: `FlightController`, `CameraController`, `InputManager`, and centralized `AssetManager` (procedural PBR canvas textures, caching/ref-counting, async session preparation, disposal).\n- **Configuration & Contracts (`src/config/`, `src/types/`)**: Ship registry (`SHIP_CONFIGS` for Interceptor, Striker, Destroyer), adaptive `GRAPHICS_PRESETS` + software WebGL detection, and reserved TypeScript contracts for future combat weapons, bot personalities (`aggressor`, `flanker`, `defender`, `ace`), and mission ranks (`S`, `A`, `B`, `C`).\n- **3D Rendering (`src/scene/`)**: `FlightCanvas` (isolated R3F `<Canvas>` with ACES Filmic tone mapping and context-loss recovery), `GameScene`, `SpaceEnvironment`, `SpeedLinesVFX`, and procedural `shipGeometry`.\n- **Audio (`src/audio/`)**: `AudioManager` using Web Audio API with zero external audio assets.\n- **UI & HUD (`src/components/`, `src/App.tsx`)**: `MainMenu`, `HangarView`, `SettingsPanel`, `LoadingScreen`, `FlightHUD`, and `PauseOverlay`.\n\n### 3. Dependencies Installed\n- `three`\n- `@types/three`\n- `@react-three/fiber`\n- `@react-three/drei`\n\n### 4. Tests Performed & Results\n- **TypeScript & Production Build** (`tsc --noEmit` + `vite build`): **Passed** with zero errors or warnings.\n- **Dev Server Check**: Restarted dev server on port 3000; HTTP `GET /` returned `200`.\n- **Automated Flight & Camera Simulation Assertions** (`tsx` harness directly exercising `FlightController` and `CameraController`): **Passed**:\n  - `W` acceleration reaches cruise speed within `maxSpeed`.\n  - `Shift` boost exceeds `1.4x` base speed, drains boost energy, and reports `BOOSTING`; releasing `Shift` regenerates boost energy after cooldown.\n  - `S` decelerates into reverse and reports `REVERSING`.\n  - Mouse delta yaw scales proportionally with `mouseSensitivity` (`75.9\302\260` at `1.0x` vs `102.7\302\260` at `2.0x`).\n  - `A` roll rotates roll angle independently without gimbal lock.\n  - Chase camera widens FOV during boost (`62.0\302\260` \342\206\222 `78.3\302\260`) and enforces distance guardrail (`11.42m`).\n- **Manual Browser Verification Note**: A headless Chromium binary is not installed in this environment, so live interactive WebGL visual rendering, Pointer Lock cursor capture, and audible Web Audio playback should be verified directly in the AI Studio preview window.\n\n### 5. Known Issues / Technical Limitations\n- **Embedded Iframe Pointer Lock**: Some sandboxed iframe environments require a direct click inside the 3D canvas after entering gameplay to acquire Pointer Lock. To ensure uninterrupted playability, the HUD displays a one-click Pointer Lock prompt whenever unlocked, and left-click-drag + arrow-key steering also function as fallbacks.\n- **Unimplemented Future Features**: Weapons firing, enemy AI, combat missions, and Striker/Destroyer unlocks are intentionally deferred to upcoming phases and clearly labeled as coming soon in the UI.\n\n### 6. Recommended Next Development Phase\n**Phase 2: Combat Core \342\200\224 Weapons, Projectiles & Enemy AI**\n1. Implement pooled laser/plasma projectile rendering (`InstancedMesh`) and weapon firing (`Left Click` / `Space`) bound to each ship\'s `weapons` config and cannon hardpoints.\n2. Add spatial hit detection, shield/hull damage feedback, explosion particle pools, and Web Audio weapon/impact sound synthesis.\n3. Implement the first enemy fighter archetypes and the four planned AI steering behaviors (`Aggressor`, `Flanker`, `Defender`, `Ace`) with HUD target lock-on brackets and lead indicators."
    thinking: "**Confirming Successful Validation**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that every flight simulation and chase camera assertion has passed without issue. The reported sensor readings are within expected parameters (headingSens1: 75.9\302\260, headingSens2: 102.7\302\260, boostFov: 78.3\302\260, camDist: 11.42m). Additionally, the TypeScript compiler has provided a clean compile with no errors.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "hgb_avTvBbi9vdIPv6mW6Q8"
    modified_response: "**STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 1: Project Foundation & Flight Prototype** has been implemented and verified.\n\n### 1. Summary of Implemented Features\n- **3D Space Environment**: Deep-space procedural GLSL nebula skybox anchored to camera coordinates, multi-spectral twinkling starfield, ringed gas giant (*Aurelia Prime*) with Fresnel atmospheric rim glow and procedural ring banding, cratered rocky moon, instanced asteroid belt, orbital navigation beacons, and a 3-point lighting rig paired with `RoomEnvironment` PMREM reflections.\n- **Player Spaceship & Hangar Chassis**: Multi-part procedural 3D PBR space fighters (`THREE.Group` with beveled wings, sculpted fuselage, armored cockpit canopy, wing cannon pods, and custom GLSL volumetric plasma exhaust plumes). The **VX-9 Vanguard (Interceptor)** is active for flight; **SR-4 Valkyrie (Striker)** and **HX-12 Aegis (Destroyer)** are inspectable in 3D in the Hangar and marked as coming soon.\n- **6DOF Arcade Flight Controller**: Quaternion-based local-space pitch, yaw, and independent roll (`A`/`D`), relative mouse steering via Pointer Lock API (with drag-to-steer and arrow-key fallbacks), forward/reverse thrust (`W`/`S`), arcade lateral velocity alignment with controlled inertia, and configurable sensitivity / invert-Y.\n- **Boost System**: Holding `Shift` multiplies speed and acceleration, intensifies engine glow and exhaust length, widens chase camera FOV, activates instanced space-dust/boost speed lines, drains boost energy, enforces a short lockout on full depletion, and regenerates energy after a cooldown.\n- **Third-Person Chase Camera**: Frame-rate-independent exponentially damped follow position and quaternion tracking, subtle turn lead/lag clamped so the fighter stays framed, dynamic boost FOV widening (`62\302\260` \342\206\222 `~78.5\302\260`), subtle boost micro-vibration, and smooth Menu/Hangar showcase orbits.\n- **Zero-Re-Render Flight HUD**: Updates velocity, hull integrity, boost energy, flight status, heading/pitch/roll readout, dynamic turn-lead reticle, and optional performance telemetry (`FPS`, frame time, draw calls, triangle count) via a `requestAnimationFrame` DOM-ref loop without per-frame React state updates. Includes collapsible control hints (`H`) and click-to-lock prompt.\n- **Menu, Hangar, Pause & Settings**: Live-3D Main Menu (`Play`, `Hangar`, `Settings`), interactive drag-to-orbit 3D Hangar with comparative ship specs, progressive Loading screen, `Esc` pause overlay (`Resume Flight`, `Settings`, `Reset Flight Position`, `Main Menu`), and locally persisted Settings (mouse sensitivity, invert pitch, camera distance, tracking responsiveness, master volume, graphics quality presets, performance overlay).\n- **Procedural Web Audio Engine**: Synthesized ion engine hum (pitch/filter tracked to velocity and throttle), afterburner boost roar + engage burst, and UI hover/click/pause sounds unlocked on user gesture with master volume control.\n\n### 2. Project Architecture\n- **Engine & Simulation (`src/engine/`)**: `FlightController`, `CameraController`, `InputManager`, and centralized `AssetManager` (procedural PBR canvas textures, caching/ref-counting, async session preparation, disposal).\n- **Configuration & Contracts (`src/config/`, `src/types/`)**: Ship registry (`SHIP_CONFIGS` for Interceptor, Striker, Destroyer), adaptive `GRAPHICS_PRESETS` + software WebGL detection, and reserved TypeScript contracts for future combat weapons, bot personalities (`aggressor`, `flanker`, `defender`, `ace`), and mission ranks (`S`, `A`, `B`, `C`).\n- **3D Rendering (`src/scene/`)**: `FlightCanvas` (isolated R3F `<Canvas>` with ACES Filmic tone mapping and context-loss recovery), `GameScene`, `SpaceEnvironment`, `SpeedLinesVFX`, and procedural `shipGeometry`.\n- **Audio (`src/audio/`)**: `AudioManager` using Web Audio API with zero external audio assets.\n- **UI & HUD (`src/components/`, `src/App.tsx`)**: `MainMenu`, `HangarView`, `SettingsPanel`, `LoadingScreen`, `FlightHUD`, and `PauseOverlay`.\n\n### 3. Dependencies Installed\n- `three`\n- `@types/three`\n- `@react-three/fiber`\n- `@react-three/drei`\n\n### 4. Tests Performed & Results\n- **TypeScript & Production Build** (`tsc --noEmit` + `vite build`): **Passed** with zero errors or warnings.\n- **Dev Server Check**: Restarted dev server on port 3000; HTTP `GET /` returned `200`.\n- **Automated Flight & Camera Simulation Assertions** (`tsx` harness directly exercising `FlightController` and `CameraController`): **Passed**:\n  - `W` acceleration reaches cruise speed within `maxSpeed`.\n  - `Shift` boost exceeds `1.4x` base speed, drains boost energy, and reports `BOOSTING`; releasing `Shift` regenerates boost energy after cooldown.\n  - `S` decelerates into reverse and reports `REVERSING`.\n  - Mouse delta yaw scales proportionally with `mouseSensitivity` (`75.9\302\260` at `1.0x` vs `102.7\302\260` at `2.0x`).\n  - `A` roll rotates roll angle independently without gimbal lock.\n  - Chase camera widens FOV during boost (`62.0\302\260` \342\206\222 `78.3\302\260`) and enforces distance guardrail (`11.42m`).\n- **Manual Browser Verification Note**: A headless Chromium binary is not installed in this environment, so live interactive WebGL visual rendering, Pointer Lock cursor capture, and audible Web Audio playback should be verified directly in the AI Studio preview window.\n\n### 5. Known Issues / Technical Limitations\n- **Embedded Iframe Pointer Lock**: Some sandboxed iframe environments require a direct click inside the 3D canvas after entering gameplay to acquire Pointer Lock. To ensure uninterrupted playability, the HUD displays a one-click Pointer Lock prompt whenever unlocked, and left-click-drag + arrow-key steering also function as fallbacks.\n- **Unimplemented Future Features**: Weapons firing, enemy AI, combat missions, and Striker/Destroyer unlocks are intentionally deferred to upcoming phases and clearly labeled as coming soon in the UI.\n\n### 6. Recommended Next Development Phase\n**Phase 2: Combat Core \342\200\224 Weapons, Projectiles & Enemy AI**\n1. Implement pooled laser/plasma projectile rendering (`InstancedMesh`) and weapon firing (`Left Click` / `Space`) bound to each ship\'s `weapons` config and cannon hardpoints.\n2. Add spatial hit detection, shield/hull damage feedback, explosion particle pools, and Web Audio weapon/impact sound synthesis.\n3. Implement the first enemy fighter archetypes and the four planned AI steering behaviors (`Aggressor`, `Flanker`, `Defender`, `Ace`) with HUD target lock-on brackets and lead indicators."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 567949997
    }
