  planner_response {
    response: "**STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 2: Combat Engine & Enemy AI Foundation** has been implemented, integrated with the existing Phase 1 flight prototype, and verified.\n\n### 1. Architecture Changes\n- **Decoupled Combat Runtime (`src/engine/combat/`)**: Added a modular, UI-independent combat layer (`CombatManager`, `ProjectilePool`, `CollisionSystem`, `HealthSystem`, `EnemyAIController`) integrated cleanly into the existing delta-time `useFrame` loop without altering W/S thrust, A/D roll, or Shift boost physics.\n- **Multiplayer-Ready Contracts (`src/types/combat.ts`)**: Defined explicit entity ownership (`EntityId`, `Faction`), `WeaponFireEvent`, `DamageEvent`, `DestructionEvent`, `HealthState`, and `CombatStats` payloads so future host-authoritative synchronization can bind directly to combat events without rewriting combat logic.\n- **Zero-Re-Render Visual & HUD Pipeline**: Pooled `InstancedMesh` energy projectiles, pooled impact/explosion VFX, pooled enemy ship rigs, and DOM-ref-driven 3D HUD target brackets all update directly from mutable engine state with zero per-frame React state updates.\n\n### 2. New and Modified Files\n- **New Files**:\n  - `src/types/combat.ts` \342\200\224 Weapons, projectiles, health, damage/destruction events, AI states, bot personality configs, combat stats, and projected HUD target marker contracts.\n  - `src/config/weapons.ts` \342\200\224 Configurable weapon profiles (`player_pulse_twin`, `enemy_pulse_aggressor`, `enemy_pulse_flanker`, `enemy_pulse_defender`, `enemy_pulse_ace`).\n  - `src/config/botPersonalities.ts` \342\200\224 Tactical profiles for `Aggressor`, `Flanker`, `Defender`, and `Ace`, plus `resolveBotDifficultyTuning` scaling reaction time, dispersion, cadence, and agility without bullet-sponge HP inflation.\n  - `src/engine/combat/HealthSystem.ts` \342\200\224 Validated health & damage application with post-destruction immunity.\n  - `src/engine/combat/ProjectilePool.ts` \342\200\224 Pre-allocated 160-slot zero-GC projectile simulator with delta-time integration and clean expiry recycling.\n  - `src/engine/combat/CollisionSystem.ts` \342\200\224 Continuous swept segment-vs-sphere collision (prevents fast laser tunneling) and ship-to-ship sphere separation.\n  - `src/engine/combat/EnemyAIController.ts` \342\200\224 7-state pilot AI (`patrol`, `acquire`, `pursue`, `engage`, `evade`, `reposition`, `destroyed`) with smooth rate-limited quaternion flight and damage evasion.\n  - `src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts` \342\200\224 Orchestrates player firing, cooldown enforcement, alternating twin wing cannons, projectile convergence, swept hit detection, enemy wave spawning, combat stats, and 3D-to-HUD screen projections.\n  - `src/scene/EnemyShipRenderer.tsx` \342\200\224 Pooled hostile 3D starfighter renderer with crimson-amber livery, thrusters, and impact flash feedback.\n  - `src/scene/CombatVFX.tsx` \342\200\224 Pooled `InstancedMesh` player/enemy plasma bolts, 220-particle impact/explosion spark pool, and 12-slot expanding shockwave/core detonation pool.\n- **Modified Files**:\n  - `src/types/game.ts` \342\200\224 Extended `FlightTelemetry` with 3D aim/boresight screen coordinates, firing/cooldown state, hit/kill/damage timers, muzzle flash timers, `combatStats`, and `enemyMarkers`.\n  - `src/engine/InputManager.ts` \342\200\224 Added continuous Left Mouse Button firing (plus `Space` secondary fire) and raised pointer-lock spike cap from `120px` to `220px` so broad aiming sweeps are not clipped.\n  - `src/engine/FlightController.ts` \342\200\224 Upgraded mouse steering to an expanded gimbaled aiming envelope (`MAX_AIM_YAW_RAD = 23\302\260`, `MAX_AIM_PITCH_RAD = 17\302\260`) with non-linear micro-precision shaping and roll-stabilized world aim.\n  - `src/engine/CameraController.ts` \342\200\224 Blended chase look target gently toward the expanded aim ray and added brief combat shock impulse.\n  - `src/audio/AudioManager.ts` \342\200\224 Added procedural Web Audio combat sounds (`playPlayerLaser`, distance-attenuated `playEnemyLaser`, `playImpactHit`, `playPlayerDamage`, and `playExplosion`) with rate-limiting.\n  - `src/scene/GameScene.tsx` & `src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx` \342\200\224 Integrated `CombatManager`, wing muzzle flash sprites, `EnemyShipRenderer`, `CombatVFX`, audio hooks, and player destruction handling.\n  - `src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`, `src/components/MainMenu.tsx`, `src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Added true 3D-projected aiming reticle + boresight tether, hit/kill crosshairs, pooled 3D enemy brackets + health bars + off-screen edge indicators + primary target lead pip, weapon status, combat stats, peripheral crimson damage vignette, and Hull Destroyed relaunch modal.\n\n### 3. Implemented Combat Features\n- **Primary Weapon**: Hold `Left Mouse Button` (or `Space`) to fire alternating left/right wing Twin Pulse Cannons (`7.5 rounds/sec`, `520 m/s`, `20 damage`, `2.1s` lifetime), with wing muzzle flashes, procedural plasma fire audio, and dynamic convergence onto the exact 3D aiming reticle ray (and active locked target distance).\n- **Pooled Projectiles & Swept Collisions**: 160 pooled projectiles checked via swept segment-sphere intersection; projectiles deactivate on first valid hit, never damage their own shooter/faction, and cannot damage already-destroyed ships.\n- **Health, Damage & Destruction**: Player and enemy health tracking, crimson peripheral HUD flash + damage thud + camera impulse when hit, cyan/orange hit & kill reticle crosshairs, pooled spark/shockwave ship explosions, wave progression, and instant fighter relaunch if player hull reaches zero.\n\n### 4. Bot AI Capabilities\n- **7-State Finite State Machine**: `patrol` \342\206\222 `acquire` \342\206\222 `pursue` \342\206\222 `engage` \342\206\222 `evade` \342\206\222 `reposition` \342\206\222 `destroyed`.\n- **Smooth Quaternion Flight**: Bots turn smoothly with clamped angular turn rates, bank visually into turns, maintain wingman separation, lead moving targets during timed burst fire, jink evasively (`evade`) upon taking damage, and break off to `reposition` when closing inside minimum safe distance.\n- **4 Configurable Personalities**: Wave 1 deploys `Aggressor` and `Flanker` wings; Wave 2 introduces `Defender`; Wave 3+ deploys all four including `Ace`, with difficulty scaling reaction time, spread, cadence, and agility.\n\n### 5. Mouse Aiming Improvements\n- **Root Cause Identified**: Phase 1 converted raw `mouseDelta / dt` into a velocity impulse clamped to a tight `maxYaw/maxPitch` ceiling that immediately decayed toward zero between mouse events, discarding fast sweeps while the HUD reticle was boxed within `\302\26126px \303\227 \302\26120px`.\n- **Expanded Gimbaled Aiming Envelope**: Mouse deltas now feed a non-linear precision shaper (fine `0.85x` response for `\342\211\244 6px` micro-movements; progressive expansion for broad sweeps) driving a roll-stabilized elliptical aiming envelope (`\302\26123\302\260` yaw, `\302\26117\302\260` pitch off-boresight). The ship smoothly chases and consumes the offset using local-space quaternions (zero gimbal lock, zero endless spin when mouse stops), while weapons and the 3D-projected HUD reticle share the exact same world aim ray (`dot = 0.999999`).\n\n### 6. Performance Measurements & Tests Performed\n- **TypeScript & Production Build**: `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` both **passed** with zero errors.\n- **Dev Server Check**: Restarted dev server on port 3000; HTTP `GET /` returned `200`.\n- **Automated Phase 2 Simulation & Benchmark Suite (`tsx` harness)**: **All assertions passed**:\n  - **Micro-aim precision**: `2px` mouse nudge produced `0.230\302\260` aim offset.\n  - **Expanded aiming range**: Sustained sweep expanded cleanly to `16.6\302\260` yaw / `10.3\302\260` pitch off-boresight (within `\302\26123\302\260 / \302\26117\302\260` envelope) and settled back to `< 0.01 rad` with zero overshoot when mouse stopped.\n  - **Reticle-to-weapon alignment**: Alignment dot product between fired bolt vector and 3D aim convergence target = `0.999999`.\n  - **Continuous fire rate clamping**: `7` shots fired in `1.0s` (configured `7.5/s`).\n  - **Hit detection, self-damage immunity & destruction**: `4` hits destroyed an `80 HP` enemy, player took `0` self-damage, and `applyDamage` returned `applied: false` post-destruction.\n  - **Enemy AI loop**: Observed transitions across `acquire`, `pursue`, `engage`, and `reposition`, with `24` enemy projectiles fired over 6 simulated seconds; verified `Ace` difficulty 5 reduces spread and reaction time relative to difficulty 1.\n  - **CPU Simulation Benchmark**: `1,000` full frames (flight + chase camera + combat + active projectiles + AI + collisions + 3D projections) completed in **`73.30 ms`** total (**`0.0733 ms/frame`** average simulation time).\n\n### 7. Known Limitations\n- **Live GPU Frame Rate Verification**: This sandbox does not include a headless Chromium binary with GPU acceleration, so while CPU simulation cost (`0.0733 ms/frame`) and build/server health are measured and verified, actual GPU FPS, Pointer Lock feel, and live Web Audio acoustics should be verified in the AI Studio preview window (an optional live FPS / draw-call readout is built into `Settings \342\206\222 Show Performance Stats`).\n- **Deferred Scope**: Five-mission campaign progression, S/A/B/C ranking, LocalStorage ship unlock progression, secondary weapons/missiles, and multiplayer networking are intentionally deferred to subsequent phases.\n\n### 8. Recommended Next Phase\n**Phase 3: Mission Campaign, Progression & Multi-Ship Unlocks**\n1. Build the 5-mission progressive campaign structure with sector objectives, wave scripting, mission briefing/debriefing screens, and performance-based `S / A / B / C` ranking.\n2. Enable playable switching between **Interceptor**, **Striker**, and **Destroyer** with distinct weapon loadouts and LocalStorage progression unlocks.\n3. Add radar/minimap orientation cues and shield recharge mechanics if desired for higher-difficulty Ace encounters."
    message_id: "Jgr_apTbIpigz7IPxJrduA4"
    modified_response: "**STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 2: Combat Engine & Enemy AI Foundation** has been implemented, integrated with the existing Phase 1 flight prototype, and verified.\n\n### 1. Architecture Changes\n- **Decoupled Combat Runtime (`src/engine/combat/`)**: Added a modular, UI-independent combat layer (`CombatManager`, `ProjectilePool`, `CollisionSystem`, `HealthSystem`, `EnemyAIController`) integrated cleanly into the existing delta-time `useFrame` loop without altering W/S thrust, A/D roll, or Shift boost physics.\n- **Multiplayer-Ready Contracts (`src/types/combat.ts`)**: Defined explicit entity ownership (`EntityId`, `Faction`), `WeaponFireEvent`, `DamageEvent`, `DestructionEvent`, `HealthState`, and `CombatStats` payloads so future host-authoritative synchronization can bind directly to combat events without rewriting combat logic.\n- **Zero-Re-Render Visual & HUD Pipeline**: Pooled `InstancedMesh` energy projectiles, pooled impact/explosion VFX, pooled enemy ship rigs, and DOM-ref-driven 3D HUD target brackets all update directly from mutable engine state with zero per-frame React state updates.\n\n### 2. New and Modified Files\n- **New Files**:\n  - `src/types/combat.ts` \342\200\224 Weapons, projectiles, health, damage/destruction events, AI states, bot personality configs, combat stats, and projected HUD target marker contracts.\n  - `src/config/weapons.ts` \342\200\224 Configurable weapon profiles (`player_pulse_twin`, `enemy_pulse_aggressor`, `enemy_pulse_flanker`, `enemy_pulse_defender`, `enemy_pulse_ace`).\n  - `src/config/botPersonalities.ts` \342\200\224 Tactical profiles for `Aggressor`, `Flanker`, `Defender`, and `Ace`, plus `resolveBotDifficultyTuning` scaling reaction time, dispersion, cadence, and agility without bullet-sponge HP inflation.\n  - `src/engine/combat/HealthSystem.ts` \342\200\224 Validated health & damage application with post-destruction immunity.\n  - `src/engine/combat/ProjectilePool.ts` \342\200\224 Pre-allocated 160-slot zero-GC projectile simulator with delta-time integration and clean expiry recycling.\n  - `src/engine/combat/CollisionSystem.ts` \342\200\224 Continuous swept segment-vs-sphere collision (prevents fast laser tunneling) and ship-to-ship sphere separation.\n  - `src/engine/combat/EnemyAIController.ts` \342\200\224 7-state pilot AI (`patrol`, `acquire`, `pursue`, `engage`, `evade`, `reposition`, `destroyed`) with smooth rate-limited quaternion flight and damage evasion.\n  - `src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts` \342\200\224 Orchestrates player firing, cooldown enforcement, alternating twin wing cannons, projectile convergence, swept hit detection, enemy wave spawning, combat stats, and 3D-to-HUD screen projections.\n  - `src/scene/EnemyShipRenderer.tsx` \342\200\224 Pooled hostile 3D starfighter renderer with crimson-amber livery, thrusters, and impact flash feedback.\n  - `src/scene/CombatVFX.tsx` \342\200\224 Pooled `InstancedMesh` player/enemy plasma bolts, 220-particle impact/explosion spark pool, and 12-slot expanding shockwave/core detonation pool.\n- **Modified Files**:\n  - `src/types/game.ts` \342\200\224 Extended `FlightTelemetry` with 3D aim/boresight screen coordinates, firing/cooldown state, hit/kill/damage timers, muzzle flash timers, `combatStats`, and `enemyMarkers`.\n  - `src/engine/InputManager.ts` \342\200\224 Added continuous Left Mouse Button firing (plus `Space` secondary fire) and raised pointer-lock spike cap from `120px` to `220px` so broad aiming sweeps are not clipped.\n  - `src/engine/FlightController.ts` \342\200\224 Upgraded mouse steering to an expanded gimbaled aiming envelope (`MAX_AIM_YAW_RAD = 23\302\260`, `MAX_AIM_PITCH_RAD = 17\302\260`) with non-linear micro-precision shaping and roll-stabilized world aim.\n  - `src/engine/CameraController.ts` \342\200\224 Blended chase look target gently toward the expanded aim ray and added brief combat shock impulse.\n  - `src/audio/AudioManager.ts` \342\200\224 Added procedural Web Audio combat sounds (`playPlayerLaser`, distance-attenuated `playEnemyLaser`, `playImpactHit`, `playPlayerDamage`, and `playExplosion`) with rate-limiting.\n  - `src/scene/GameScene.tsx` & `src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx` \342\200\224 Integrated `CombatManager`, wing muzzle flash sprites, `EnemyShipRenderer`, `CombatVFX`, audio hooks, and player destruction handling.\n  - `src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`, `src/components/MainMenu.tsx`, `src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Added true 3D-projected aiming reticle + boresight tether, hit/kill crosshairs, pooled 3D enemy brackets + health bars + off-screen edge indicators + primary target lead pip, weapon status, combat stats, peripheral crimson damage vignette, and Hull Destroyed relaunch modal.\n\n### 3. Implemented Combat Features\n- **Primary Weapon**: Hold `Left Mouse Button` (or `Space`) to fire alternating left/right wing Twin Pulse Cannons (`7.5 rounds/sec`, `520 m/s`, `20 damage`, `2.1s` lifetime), with wing muzzle flashes, procedural plasma fire audio, and dynamic convergence onto the exact 3D aiming reticle ray (and active locked target distance).\n- **Pooled Projectiles & Swept Collisions**: 160 pooled projectiles checked via swept segment-sphere intersection; projectiles deactivate on first valid hit, never damage their own shooter/faction, and cannot damage already-destroyed ships.\n- **Health, Damage & Destruction**: Player and enemy health tracking, crimson peripheral HUD flash + damage thud + camera impulse when hit, cyan/orange hit & kill reticle crosshairs, pooled spark/shockwave ship explosions, wave progression, and instant fighter relaunch if player hull reaches zero.\n\n### 4. Bot AI Capabilities\n- **7-State Finite State Machine**: `patrol` \342\206\222 `acquire` \342\206\222 `pursue` \342\206\222 `engage` \342\206\222 `evade` \342\206\222 `reposition` \342\206\222 `destroyed`.\n- **Smooth Quaternion Flight**: Bots turn smoothly with clamped angular turn rates, bank visually into turns, maintain wingman separation, lead moving targets during timed burst fire, jink evasively (`evade`) upon taking damage, and break off to `reposition` when closing inside minimum safe distance.\n- **4 Configurable Personalities**: Wave 1 deploys `Aggressor` and `Flanker` wings; Wave 2 introduces `Defender`; Wave 3+ deploys all four including `Ace`, with difficulty scaling reaction time, spread, cadence, and agility.\n\n### 5. Mouse Aiming Improvements\n- **Root Cause Identified**: Phase 1 converted raw `mouseDelta / dt` into a velocity impulse clamped to a tight `maxYaw/maxPitch` ceiling that immediately decayed toward zero between mouse events, discarding fast sweeps while the HUD reticle was boxed within `\302\26126px \303\227 \302\26120px`.\n- **Expanded Gimbaled Aiming Envelope**: Mouse deltas now feed a non-linear precision shaper (fine `0.85x` response for `\342\211\244 6px` micro-movements; progressive expansion for broad sweeps) driving a roll-stabilized elliptical aiming envelope (`\302\26123\302\260` yaw, `\302\26117\302\260` pitch off-boresight). The ship smoothly chases and consumes the offset using local-space quaternions (zero gimbal lock, zero endless spin when mouse stops), while weapons and the 3D-projected HUD reticle share the exact same world aim ray (`dot = 0.999999`).\n\n### 6. Performance Measurements & Tests Performed\n- **TypeScript & Production Build**: `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` both **passed** with zero errors.\n- **Dev Server Check**: Restarted dev server on port 3000; HTTP `GET /` returned `200`.\n- **Automated Phase 2 Simulation & Benchmark Suite (`tsx` harness)**: **All assertions passed**:\n  - **Micro-aim precision**: `2px` mouse nudge produced `0.230\302\260` aim offset.\n  - **Expanded aiming range**: Sustained sweep expanded cleanly to `16.6\302\260` yaw / `10.3\302\260` pitch off-boresight (within `\302\26123\302\260 / \302\26117\302\260` envelope) and settled back to `< 0.01 rad` with zero overshoot when mouse stopped.\n  - **Reticle-to-weapon alignment**: Alignment dot product between fired bolt vector and 3D aim convergence target = `0.999999`.\n  - **Continuous fire rate clamping**: `7` shots fired in `1.0s` (configured `7.5/s`).\n  - **Hit detection, self-damage immunity & destruction**: `4` hits destroyed an `80 HP` enemy, player took `0` self-damage, and `applyDamage` returned `applied: false` post-destruction.\n  - **Enemy AI loop**: Observed transitions across `acquire`, `pursue`, `engage`, and `reposition`, with `24` enemy projectiles fired over 6 simulated seconds; verified `Ace` difficulty 5 reduces spread and reaction time relative to difficulty 1.\n  - **CPU Simulation Benchmark**: `1,000` full frames (flight + chase camera + combat + active projectiles + AI + collisions + 3D projections) completed in **`73.30 ms`** total (**`0.0733 ms/frame`** average simulation time).\n\n### 7. Known Limitations\n- **Live GPU Frame Rate Verification**: This sandbox does not include a headless Chromium binary with GPU acceleration, so while CPU simulation cost (`0.0733 ms/frame`) and build/server health are measured and verified, actual GPU FPS, Pointer Lock feel, and live Web Audio acoustics should be verified in the AI Studio preview window (an optional live FPS / draw-call readout is built into `Settings \342\206\222 Show Performance Stats`).\n- **Deferred Scope**: Five-mission campaign progression, S/A/B/C ranking, LocalStorage ship unlock progression, secondary weapons/missiles, and multiplayer networking are intentionally deferred to subsequent phases.\n\n### 8. Recommended Next Phase\n**Phase 3: Mission Campaign, Progression & Multi-Ship Unlocks**\n1. Build the 5-mission progressive campaign structure with sector objectives, wave scripting, mission briefing/debriefing screens, and performance-based `S / A / B / C` ranking.\n2. Enable playable switching between **Interceptor**, **Striker**, and **Destroyer** with distinct weapon loadouts and LocalStorage progression unlocks.\n3. Add radar/minimap orientation cues and shield recharge mechanics if desired for higher-difficulty Ace encounters."
