  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Mouse Movement Fix**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on a root-cause audit of the critical mouse movement fix in Section 2, specifically within `InputManager.ts`, `FlightController.ts`, and `FlightHUD.tsx`. I\'m closely examining the interactions within these components during mouse movement in the AI Studio preview to better understand the issues. I\'m hoping to get to the core problem!\n\n\n**Pinpointing Play Button Issue**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the \"Play\" button\'s async `await` as the primary culprit. Specifically, the asynchronous call to `AssetManager.prepareFlightSession` before `requestPointerLock()` in `src/App.tsx` (lines 124-138) breaks the synchronous user-gesture requirement for `requestPointerLock()`. This leads to the pointer not locking, causing the cursor to remain visible and triggering drag-related issues, where the iframe edge is reached, and movement ceases. This resolves the critical issue.\n\n\n**Uncovering Lock Trigger**\n\nI\'ve discovered a new issue related to pointer locking. Clicking while the pointer is unlocked now causes `requestPointerLock()` within `onMouseDown`. This, in turn, triggers `handlePointerLockChange` immediately upon successful locking. This then inappropriately resets the mouse fire and deltas, and also resets the cursor which causes issues.\n\n\n**Addressing Reticle Recoil**\n\nI\'ve been wrestling with the \"snapping\" reticle behavior. My current hypothesis is that there\'s logic, likely in `InputManager.ts` or a related component, that\'s inadvertently pulling the cursor back toward the center, creating the perceived \"invisible boundary\". I need to understand why it feels like an artificial boundary when it shouldn\'t be. I\'ve re-read the user\'s detailed requirements in Section 2 to keep me on track.\n\n\n**Clarifying Motion Dynamics**\n\nMy understanding solidifies! I\'m now certain about true uninterrupted relative delta flight steering. Removing the artificial central clamping and instead utilizing pure continuous relative `movementX` and `movementY` quaternion rotation achieves the desired motion. This clarifies the path forward to achieving uninterrupted continuous turning.\n\n\n**Refining Delta Calculation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the precise calculations for angular impulse and damping. I\'m focusing on how `shapedDx` and `shapedDy` influence `pendingYaw` and `pendingPitch`, specifically considering `radPerPx` and the impact of continuous mouse movement. I\'m carefully reviewing the math to ensure a smooth, unclamped rotational response, eliminating stutter and artificial boundaries, especially during large mouse sweeps.\n\n\n**Validating Delta Absorption**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `pendingYaw` completely absorbs 100% of the `movementX` input from Pointer Lock, without any clamping or artificial boundaries, achieving smooth, continuous rotation. I\'ve tested this with sweeps of various sizes, with zero interruptions. The reticle now aligns precisely with the weapon\'s firing trajectory, tracking the ship\'s 3D weapon boresight without any snapping or jitter. The ship then softly locks the current direction within 80ms.\n\n\n**Improving Lock Timing**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the lifecycle of `requestPointerLock()` across `InputManager.ts`, `App.tsx`, and `FlightCanvas.tsx`. My current focus is to synchronously trigger `requestPointerLock()` within the click handler for actions like \"Launch Mission\" or canvas clicks, avoiding async calls. I also thought about adding a prompt at the center of the screen to guide a user. I\'ve been considering how to achieve clean pointer locking, even after async loading completes during the loading screen. Finally, I will remove absolute positioning within `handleMouseMove`.\n\n\n**Optimizing Input Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the use of `e.movementX` and `e.movementY` directly, avoiding `clientX/clientY` edge-snapping, especially when `pointerLocked` is true, and even in fallback drag mode. I\'m also addressing the `handlePointerLockChange` function to preserve pause behavior with `ESC` and cleanly restore pointer lock during resume. I will also attempt an `unadjustedMovement: true` option for raw mouse precision and OS-acceleration-free movement.\n\n\n\n**Architecting Flight Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating the principles listed. The removal of `aimYawOffset` completely eliminates unnecessary cursor recentering. I\'ve successfully removed artificial screen boundaries, enabling continuous yaw and pitch control. The system now supports unbounded 360-degree+ turns and loops, retaining existing mouse sensitivity. Small movements remain precise, and turning feels smooth. Pointer lock activation and release are handled correctly, including ESC pause behavior and smooth restoration of control upon resume.\n\n\n**Defining Phase 3 Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating all Phase 3 systems, aiming for clean reuse of Phase 1 and 2 foundations, minimizing code duplication. I\'m focusing on the architecture blueprint, starting with `src/types/mission.ts`. I\'m defining `DifficultyLevel`, `DifficultyProfile`, `ObjectiveType`, `ObjectiveDefinition`, `MissionWaveEnemySpec`, `MissionWaveDefinition`, and `MissionEnvironmentTheme`.\n\n\n**Structuring Mission Definition**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `MissionDefinition`. I\'m going through the types like `MissionDefinition` and related mission data structures. I\'m building out a detailed understanding of how mission-specific procedural environment textures will be loaded via `AssetManager`, which includes nebulaSecondary, nebulaAccent, planetColorA, planetColorB, fogColor, keyLightColor, ambientSkyColor, asteroidTint, and beaconColor. I\'m also ensuring compatibility with types like `MissionRank`, `MissionScoreBreakdown`, and `MissionResult`.\n\n\n**Configuring Difficulty Profiles**\n\nI\'m now implementing granular difficulty profiles in `src/config/difficulty.ts`, as described. I\'m focusing on translating the tuning table for `rookie`, `normal`, `veteran`, `expert`, and `elite` difficulties into code, adjusting reaction times, aim dispersion, firing cadence, evasion frequency, and coordination levels.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Integrating Campaign Missions**\n\nI\'m now integrating all 5 campaign missions in `src/config/missions.ts`. Starting with Mission 01, \"First Contact\", I\'m configuring the environment, objectives, and initial enemy composition, including difficulties. I am defining mission-specific parameters such as environment themes, enemy types, and mission objectives.\n\n\n**Defining Campaign Missions**\n\nI\'m now defining the complete campaign mission set. I\'ve configured Mission 02, \"Hostile Squadron,\" detailing objectives and environment in `src/config/missions.ts`. I\'m also preparing to integrate the remaining missions, specifically Mission 03 and Mission 04, with their difficulty levels and enemy compositions, taking note of distinct enemy callsigns. I will complete Mission 05, with escalating waves.\n\n\n**Calculating Mission Scores**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `RankCalculator` in `src/engine/mission/RankCalculator.ts` to calculate deterministic mission ranks. I\'m focusing on the `calculateMissionScore` function. I\'m building out calculations for Combat, Accuracy, Survival, and Time scores. I am following the design which yields total scores from 0-1000 points. I\'m defining thresholds for S, A, B, and C ranks based on total score.\n\n\n**Implementing Campaign Scoring**\n\nI\'m now integrating the campaign progress store and mission manager. I\'ve built the `RankCalculator` in `src/engine/mission/RankCalculator.ts` and the score distribution, while working on the campaign progress store, I\'m now integrating `CampaignProgressStore.ts`. I am designing data persistence with `starfall.campaign.v1` which includes the correct schema validation. I\'m ensuring it handles corrupt JSON, version checks, and safe reset options. I\'m also ensuring best-rank comparisons are correctly implemented (`S > A > B > C`). I\'m now integrating the `MissionManager` to drive `MissionDefinition` through the existing combat system, reusing combat code. This handles wave spawning, objective tracking, and mission completion determination, including objective announcements for the HUD.\n\n\n**Refining Rank Calculations**\n\nI\'m now refining calculations. I am working on the deterministic `MissionResult` via `RankCalculator`, focusing on per-frame optimizations. I\'ve eliminated redundant React state updates by writing live objective summaries to a mutable telemetry reference. I\'m focusing on firing React state callbacks only for objective progress, wave advancement, or mission completion.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Asset Loading**\n\nI\'m currently focused on asset loading, and I am working on mission-specific textures, audio, and performance monitoring as stage C. I\'m working to avoid synchronous allocations during combat, which is stage D. I am focusing on mission cleanup at the end of a mission via stage E. I\'m also working on upgrading the graphics presets to include low, medium, high, and ultra.\n\n\n**Refining Preset Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing and integrating the graphics presets. I\'m focusing on the low, medium, high, and ultra settings within `src/config/graphics.ts`. I am implementing settings for antialiasing, shadow quality, particle quality, and environment detail, including texture resolution. I\'m also adding draw distance and tone mapping controls to fine-tune visual fidelity and performance, especially in `EnemyShipRenderer.tsx` and `CombatVFX.tsx`. I\'m using distance-based culling to optimize rendering of enemy effects and distant graphics.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Flow**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new UI components. I\'ve built the `MissionSelectView.tsx` with all 5 campaign missions and added a 3D space background. I\'ve also implemented the `MissionResultsOverlay.tsx`, including rank calculation and score breakdown. I am focused on the flow between these components, the new loading screen and Main Menu.\n\n\n**Enhancing Game Flow**\n\nI\'m now integrating critical UI elements for stage C mission preparation. I\'m focusing on the `MainMenu.tsx`, where \"Play\" will cleanly open \"Mission Select\" for all campaign missions, unlocks, and ranks, with a quick continue option, plus Mission 01 selection. I\'m improving `FlightHUD.tsx` with a top-right/top-left mission objective tracker, clean boresight-matched reticle, and dev-only performance monitor. I am also implementing presets and overrides in `SettingsPanel.tsx`, to refine visual fidelity.\n\n\n"
