  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n# STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 3 Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Task Overview\nWe are building **STARFALL**, a browser-based 3D sci-fi arcade space combat game (React 19 + TypeScript + Three.js + React Three Fiber + Drei + Web Audio API).\n- **Phase 1 (Complete)**: 3D space environment, procedural multi-part PBR starfighter (`VX-9 Vanguard` Interceptor playable; `Striker` and `Destroyer` previewable in 3D Hangar), 6DOF quaternion flight controller, boost system, third-person chase camera, zero-re-render DOM-ref FlightHUD, Main Menu, Settings, Pause overlay, procedural Web Audio API sound engine.\n- **Phase 2 (Complete)**: Modular combat engine (`CombatManager`, `ProjectilePool`, `CollisionSystem`, `HealthSystem`, `EnemyAIController`), primary Twin Pulse Cannons (`LMB`/`Space`), 7-state Enemy Bot AI across 4 personalities (`Aggressor`, `Flanker`, `Defender`, `Ace`), pooled `InstancedMesh` bolts & explosions/sparks, combat audio, 3D HUD target brackets & lead pip.\n- **Phase 3 (ACTIVE \342\200\224 In Progress)**: Complete single-player mission campaign + critical continuous mouse turning fix + progressive asset loading + runtime performance engineering + adaptive Low/Medium/High/Ultra graphics settings + dev-only performance monitor.\n- **Scope Boundaries for Phase 3**:\n  - DO NOT implement: full 3-ship unlock economy, LAN multiplayer, invitation codes, signaling, WebRTC, or room management.\n  - Preserve existing flight acceleration, boost, roll, combat, and visual identity (deep navy, electric cyan, dark metallic surfaces).\n  - Final report MUST cover 13 explicit items: (1) Mission system architecture, (2) Five missions implemented, (3) Objective and progression systems, (4) Rank calculation rules, (5) Mouse movement root cause and exact fix, (6) Asset Manager improvements, (7) Progressive loading behavior, (8) Optimization techniques implemented, (9) Graphics settings implemented, (10) Performance measurements, (11) Tests performed, (12) Remaining issues, (13) Recommended next development phase.\n\n## 2. Progress\n\n### Completed in Phase 1 & 2 (Verified & Working)\n- Installed packages: `three`, `@types/three`, `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`.\n- Updated `/metadata.json`, `/index.html` (Oxanium, Plus Jakarta Sans, JetBrains Mono fonts), `/src/index.css`.\n- Existing working files:\n  - `/src/types/game.ts`, `/src/types/combat.ts`\n  - `/src/config/ships.ts`, `/src/config/graphics.ts`, `/src/config/weapons.ts`, `/src/config/botPersonalities.ts`\n  - `/src/engine/AssetManager.ts`, `/src/engine/InputManager.ts`, `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `/src/engine/CameraController.ts`\n  - `/src/engine/combat/HealthSystem.ts`, `/src/engine/combat/ProjectilePool.ts`, `/src/engine/combat/CollisionSystem.ts`, `/src/engine/combat/EnemyAIController.ts`, `/src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts`\n  - `/src/audio/AudioManager.ts`\n  - `/src/scene/shipGeometry.ts`, `/src/scene/SpaceEnvironment.tsx`, `/src/scene/SpeedLinesVFX.tsx`, `/src/scene/EnemyShipRenderer.tsx`, `/src/scene/CombatVFX.tsx`, `/src/scene/GameScene.tsx`, `/src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx`\n  - `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`, `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, `/src/components/HangarView.tsx`, `/src/components/MainMenu.tsx`, `/src/components/PauseOverlay.tsx`, `/src/components/LoadingScreen.tsx`\n  - `/src/App.tsx`\n\n### Completed in Phase 3 (Batch 1 Created \342\200\224 Not Yet Wired/Compiled)\nCreated 5 new Phase 3 mission foundation files:\n1. `/src/types/mission.ts` \342\200\224 Full contracts: `DifficultyLevel` (`rookie | normal | veteran | expert | elite`), `DifficultyProfile`, `ObjectiveType` (`eliminate_all | survive_duration | defeat_target | survive_waves`), `ObjectiveDefinition`, `ObjectiveRuntimeState`, `MissionWaveEnemySpec`, `MissionWaveDefinition`, `MissionEnvironmentTheme`, `MissionDefinition`, `MissionScoreBreakdown`, `MissionResult`, `MissionProgressRecord`, `CampaignSaveData`, `MissionHudSnapshot`.\n2. `/src/config/difficulty.ts` \342\200\224 `DIFFICULTY_PROFILES` scaling `reactionTimeScale`, `aimSpreadScale`, `agilityScale`, `speedScale`, `fireCadenceScale`, `evadeScale`, `coordinationIntervalSec`, `burstPressureScale` (no bullet-sponge HP/damage inflation).\n3. `/src/config/missions.ts` \342\200\224 `CAMPAIGN_MISSIONS` with all 5 required missions, each with distinct `MissionEnvironmentTheme`:\n   - `mission-01`: **First Contact** (`rookie`, 2 aggressors, `eliminate_all`, unlocked by default).\n   - `mission-02`: **Hostile Squadron** (`normal`, 4 mixed bots: 2 aggressors, 1 flanker, 1 defender, `eliminate_all`).\n   - `mission-03`: **Ambush** (`veteran`, 5 bots surrounding player on multiple 3D vectors, `survive_duration` 20s + `eliminate_all` 5).\n   - `mission-04`: **Ace Hunters** (`expert`, 3 elite pilots: 2 `ace` + 1 `flanker`, `eliminate_all`).\n   - `mission-05`: **Final Stand** (`elite`, 3 escalating waves culminating in named Ace commander `SOVEREIGN-ONE`, `survive_waves` 3 + `defeat_target` `SOVEREIGN-ONE`).\n4. `/src/engine/mission/RankCalculator.ts` \342\200\224 Deterministic `calculateMissionScore()` (0\342\200\2231000 pts: Combat 400 + Accuracy 250 + Survival 200 + Time 150; `S >= 820`, `A >= 660`, `B >= 480`, `C < 480`) + `isBetterRank()`.\n5. `/src/engine/mission/CampaignProgressStore.ts` \342\200\224 Safe LocalStorage persistence (`starfall.campaign.v1`) with schema version check, corrupt-JSON recovery, `isMissionUnlocked()`, and `recordMissionOutcome()` preserving best rank, best score, and best time.\n\n### Skills Read in Session\n- `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md` + `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/5_threejs_3d_spatial.md`\n- `/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md` + `references/fundamentals.md`, `references/materials.md`, `references/shaders.md`\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n\n### Critical Mouse Turning Root Causes Identified (Section 2)\nTwo concrete bugs in Phase 2 caused screen-edge / snap-back interruption:\n1. **Async Pointer Lock Failure**: `App.tsx` called `inputRef.current.requestPointerLock()` *after* `await AssetManager.prepareFlightSession(...)`, which breaks the browser\'s synchronous user-gesture requirement for Pointer Lock. When Pointer Lock failed silently, `InputManager` fell back to `clientX - lastDragX` absolute coordinates, hitting physical screen/iframe boundaries.\n2. **Artificial Gimbal Clamp & Auto-Recenter Pullback**: Phase 2\'s `FlightController` clamped `aimYawOffset`/`aimPitchOffset` to an ellipse (`MAX_AIM_YAW_RAD = 23\302\260`, `MAX_AIM_PITCH_RAD = 17\302\260`) and continuously subtracted `stepYaw`/`stepPitch` back toward center (`aimYawOffset -= stepYaw`), which both clipped large mouse sweeps and visually pulled the reticle back toward center like a cursor snapping back.\n\n### Exact Mouse Fix Design (To Implement)\n- **`FlightController.ts`**: Remove `aimYawOffset`/`aimPitchOffset` radial clamping and recentering pullback entirely. Use **unbounded continuous relative-delta quaternion rotation**: accumulate `shapedDx * radPerPx` / `shapedDy * radPerPx` into smooth angular velocity / pending rotation buffer with zero boundary cap and zero snap-back. Keep fine non-linear precision for small deltas (`|delta| <= 5px`) and full linear throughput for continuous large sweeps (360\302\260+ uninterrupted yaw & pitch loops with pure local-space quaternions). `getAimDirectionWorld()` points directly along ship forward (`-Z`), matching the 3D-projected in-game boresight reticle 1:1 with zero artificial cursor recentering.\n- **`InputManager.ts`**: Use Pointer Lock `e.movementX`/`e.movementY` exclusively for continuous turning; request `{ unadjustedMovement: true }` with standard fallback; remove `120px/220px` low caps (only guard extreme browser-bug spikes `> 600px`); never depend on absolute `clientX/clientY` for continuous turning; do not fire a stray shot on the click that engages Pointer Lock; cleanly preserve `ESC` pause and restore Pointer Lock synchronously on Resume click and canvas click.\n- **`App.tsx` / `LoadingScreen.tsx`**: Trigger synchronous `requestPointerLock()` directly inside click handlers (\"Resume Flight\", canvas click-to-engage overlay, or \"Enter Flight\" after mission load if Pointer Lock was not held).\n\n### Environment Note\n- Sandbox has Node v22.23.2 + `npx tsx` + dev server on port 3000 (`curl http://localhost:3000/` returns `200`).\n- No headless Chromium/Playwright binary is installed in this sandbox; verify builds via `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) and verify runtime simulation/physics/missions/asset loading/performance thoroughly via `npx tsx` automated test suites (clearly distinguishing automated tests from manual browser GPU verification in the final report).\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- In Phase 2, `tsc --noEmit` caught `targetRoleRef` typed as `HTMLSpanElement` attached to a `<div>` in `src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`. Fixed by changing ref type to `HTMLDivElement`. Both `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` subsequently passed with zero errors.\n- No unresolved errors exist currently (Batch 1 of Phase 3 has not been compiled yet).\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Phase 3 Batch 1 (`src/types/mission.ts`, `src/config/difficulty.ts`, `src/config/missions.ts`, `src/engine/mission/RankCalculator.ts`, `src/engine/mission/CampaignProgressStore.ts`) is written on disk.\n- All remaining Phase 3 engine, scene, graphics, and UI modules still need to be implemented and wired together.\n- Remember key Three.js/Frontend constraints:\n  - Zero `backdrop-filter`/`backdrop-blur` over WebGL canvas.\n  - Zero decorative pulsing dots or static pill boxes around metadata.\n  - Zero per-frame React state updates in `useFrame` or HUD loops; only fire React state updates on discrete events (objective progress, wave change, mission end, loading progress, menu transitions).\n  - Clean disposal of GPU geometries/materials/textures; keep shared assets alive while referenced; dispose mission-specific assets in Stage E cleanup.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n\n### Step 1: Mission Runtime, Difficulty-Aware AI & Combat Integration\n1. **Create `/src/engine/mission/MissionManager.ts`**:\n   - Accepts a `MissionDefinition` and drives `CombatManager` waves (spawning exact wave enemy specs, callsigns, shipIds, personalities, offsets, priority boss flags, and `DifficultyProfile`).\n   - Tracks all 4 objective types (`eliminate_all`, `survive_duration`, `defeat_target`, `survive_waves`), completion/failure conditions, elapsed mission time, and immediate HUD announcements (`announcement`, `announcementKind`).\n   - Computes deterministic `MissionResult` via `RankCalculator` on victory or failure.\n   - Emits discrete React callback (`onMissionHudChange`, `onMissionComplete`) ONLY when objectives/waves/status change (zero per-frame React renders).\n2. **Update `/src/config/botPersonalities.ts` & `/src/engine/combat/EnemyAIController.ts`**:\n   - Accept `DifficultyProfile` (from `DIFFICULTY_PROFILES`) so Rookie/Normal/Veteran/Expert/Elite meaningfully alter reaction time, aim dispersion, movement agility/speed, firing cadence, burst pressure, evasion responsiveness, and squad coordination interval.\n   - Add coordinated flank-flip / focus pressure timer driven by `difficultyProfile.coordinationIntervalSec`.\n3. **Update `/src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts`**:\n   - Support mission-driven wave spawning (`loadMissionWave(wave, difficultyProfile, playerPos)` alongside existing skirmish fallback), track `isPriorityTarget` on `EnemyEntity` (with optional `hullBonus` for final Ace boss), expose active enemy/projectile counts for dev performance monitor, and notify `MissionManager` on enemy destruction / player destruction.\n\n### Step 2: Critical Mouse Movement Fix (Section 2)\n4. **Update `/src/engine/InputManager.ts`**:\n   - Pure relative `e.movementX` / `e.movementY` Pointer Lock input (`unadjustedMovement: true` with fallback); remove absolute coordinate dependency and low movement caps; prevent firing a stray laser shot on the first click that acquires Pointer Lock; preserve `ESC` pause and synchronous `requestPointerLock()` restoration.\n5. **Update `/src/engine/FlightController.ts` & `/src/engine/CameraController.ts`**:\n   - Replace clamped/auto-recentering `aimYawOffset`/`aimPitchOffset` with unbounded continuous relative-delta quaternion rotation (fine micro-precision curve + smooth exponential damping + zero screen-edge / center-box clamping + zero snap-back).\n   - Keep `W/S` thrust, `A/D` roll, and `Shift` boost unchanged.\n   - Ensure `getAimDirectionWorld()` aligns with ship forward `-Z` so the 3D-projected in-game virtual reticle always matches true weapon firing direction without artificial snap-back, and chase camera tracks smoothly through arbitrary 360\302\260 continuous turns & loops.\n\n### Step 3: Progressive Asset Loading (Stages A\342\200\223E) & Adaptive Graphics (Low/Medium/High/Ultra)\n6. **Update `/src/config/graphics.ts` & `/src/types/game.ts` & `/src/config/ships.ts`**:\n   - Expand `GraphicsQuality` to `\'low\' | \'medium\' | \'high\' | \'ultra\'`.\n   - Add granular graphics settings to `GameSettings`: `graphicsQuality`, `resolutionScale` (0.65\342\200\2231.0 multiplier), `shadowQuality` (`\'off\' | \'low\' | \'medium\' | \'high\'`), `particleQuality` (`\'low\' | \'medium\' | \'high\'`), `environmentDetail` (`\'low\' | \'medium\' | \'high\'`), `drawDistance` (2000\342\200\2235200), `antialias` (boolean), `postGlowEnabled` (boolean). Selecting a preset populates these cleanly, and individual tweaks actually modify Three.js rendering!\n   - Add `missionHud` / `activeProjectiles` / `activeParticles` / `activeEnemies` / `lastAssetLoadMs` / `cachedAssetCount` fields to `FlightTelemetry` for dev-only performance monitoring.\n   - Add `\'mission-select\'` to `MenuSection` and `\'results\'` to `GamePhase`.\n7. **Upgrade `/src/engine/AssetManager.ts`**:\n   - Implement explicit 5-stage progressive loading with typed asset IDs, reference counting, caching, abort/cancellation support, error recovery (`simulateFailure` optional test hook or real error catch), load-time telemetry, and safe disposal:\n     - **Stage A (Boot)**: Minimal shared sprite (`shared:glowSprite`) only \342\200\224 do NOT generate planet/ship textures at boot.\n     - **Stage B (Hangar)**: On-demand `loadShipAssets(shipId, texRes)` + safe idle background preload of other ships.\n     - **Stage C (Mission Prep)**: `loadMissionAssets(mission, shipId, texRes, onProgress, abortSignal)` loading ship PBR maps, mission-specific themed planet/moon/asteroid textures (`mission:${env.id}:env`), weapon/VFX assets, and audio warmup \342\200\224 reporting granular progress stages and measuring `lastLoadDurationMs`.\n     - **Stage E (Cleanup)**: `releaseMissionAssets(envId)` safely disposing mission-specific textures while keeping shared/referenced assets intact.\n   - Expose `getDiagnostics()` returning `{ cachedResources, totalRefs, lastLoadDurationMs, loadedKeys }`.\n\n### Step 4: Rendering Performance Engineering & Mission Environments\n8. **Update `/src/scene/SpaceEnvironment.tsx`**:\n   - Accept active `MissionEnvironmentTheme` (falling back to Mission 01 Aurelia theme on Main Menu) and `EffectiveGraphicsConfig`.\n   - Use Stage C mission-specific textures from `AssetManager` (Stage A boot uses lightweight nebula/starfield without heavy planet texture generation until needed, or minimal boot environment).\n   - Scale nebula shader FBM octaves, shadow map size, star count, asteroid count, planet segments, and fog/light colors dynamically from graphics settings + mission theme.\n9. **Update `/src/scene/EnemyShipRenderer.tsx` & `/src/scene/CombatVFX.tsx`**:\n   - Add distance-based LOD/effect culling: hide enemy engine point lights and hit-glow sprites beyond `280m` (eliminates unnecessary dynamic lights at distance); scale particle pool caps and explosion spark counts by `particleQuality`.\n   - Expose active particle count to `telemetryRef.current.activeParticles` for the dev performance monitor.\n10. **Update `/src/scene/GameScene.tsx` & `/src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx`**:\n    - Wire `MissionManager` into `useFrame` during active mission play.\n    - Pass `missionTheme`, `graphics`, and `combat` cleanly; handle dynamic `antialias` key or DPR/shadow/drawDistance updates cleanly without leaking GPU resources.\n    - Update `telemetry.activeProjectiles`, `telemetry.activeEnemies`, `telemetry.cachedAssetCount`, `telemetry.lastAssetLoadMs`.\n\n### Step 5: Campaign UI, HUD Objectives, Loading/Error Recovery & Dev Performance Monitor\n11. **Create `/src/components/MissionSelectView.tsx`**:\n    - Lists all 5 missions with mission number (`01\342\200\22305`), name, difficulty, description, enemy/wave summary, lock status, completion status, best rank (`S/A/B/C`), best score, reward label, **Launch Mission** button, and **Main Menu** back button.\n12. **Create `/src/components/MissionResultsOverlay.tsx`**:\n    - Post-mission debrief showing Completed / Failed status, prominent `S/A/B/C` rank, deterministic score breakdown (Combat, Accuracy, Survival, Time), Enemies Defeated, Accuracy %, Time Taken, Damage Received, Next Mission Unlock banner, and functional **Next Mission**, **Retry Mission**, **Mission Select**, and **Main Menu** buttons.\n13. **Upgrade `/src/components/LoadingScreen.tsx`**:\n    - Show mission number/name, selected craft, live loading stage & percentage, **Cancel** button (aborts load & returns to Mission Select), and structured error recovery UI (**Retry Load** / **Back**) if loading fails.\n14. **Update `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`**:\n    - Add clean **Mission Objectives Panel** (live objective checkmarks, counts, survival countdown timer, boss target callsign) + non-blocking **Wave / Objective Announcement Banner**.\n    - Clean centered boresight-matched virtual aiming reticle (no rubber-band tether snapping back to center) with hit/kill confirmation crosshairs and target brackets/lead pip.\n    - Gate the extended Performance Monitor (`FPS`, frame ms, draw calls, tris, active projectiles, active particles, active enemies, asset load ms, cached resources) strictly behind `import.meta.env.DEV` (development-only, toggleable via `F3` or dev Settings toggle, hidden from normal production players).\n15. **Update `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx` & `/src/components/MainMenu.tsx` & `/src/App.tsx`**:\n    - Settings: `Low / Medium / High / Ultra` presets + working granular controls (Resolution Scale, Shadow Quality, Particle Quality, Environment Detail, Draw Distance, Anti-Aliasing) + dev-only Performance Monitor toggle.\n    - Main Menu: **Play** opens **Mission Select** (or shows Campaign progress summary + quick access to all 5 missions), preserving **Hangar** and **Settings**.\n    - `App.tsx`: Wire `MissionManager`, `CampaignProgressStore`, progressive Stage A\342\200\223E `AssetManager` loading + cleanup on mission exit, synchronous Pointer Lock engagement on user gesture, and `results` phase transitions.\n\n### Step 6: Verification & Comprehensive Testing\n16. Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) \342\200\224 fix any errors.\n17. Restart dev server (`restart_dev_server`) and verify HTTP 200 on `http://localhost:3000/`.\n18. Run a thorough `npx tsx` automated verification suite testing:\n    - Continuous mouse turning (zero boundary clamp, zero snap-back across >720\302\260 continuous sweeps, micro-movement precision preserved).\n    - All 5 missions loading with exact enemy counts (`2, 4, 5, 3, 9`) and wave progression (`Mission 05` 3 waves + `SOVEREIGN-ONE`).\n    - All 4 objective types (`eliminate_all`, `survive_duration`, `defeat_target`, `survive_waves`), completion & failure states.\n    - All 5 difficulty profiles producing distinct measurable AI parameters.\n    - Deterministic `RankCalculator` (`S/A/B/C` thresholds & repeatability).\n    - `CampaignProgressStore` unlock chain (`M1 -> M2 -> M3 -> M4 -> M5`), best rank/score persistence, and corrupt JSON recovery.\n    - `AssetManager` Stage A\342\200\223E reference counting, caching, mission cleanup without disposing shared assets, and failure/abort handling.\n    - Multi-enemy + multi-projectile simulation benchmark (frame time ms across 1,000 high-intensity frames).\n19. Present the final report covering all 13 required sections from the user prompt accurately, never claiming untested features were tested.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow STARFALL Permanent Project Instructions & Phase 3 Scope Control strictly.\n- Preserve all working Phase 1 flight physics (`W/S` thrust, `A/D` roll, `Shift` boost) and Phase 2 combat foundations.\n- Do not add backend/multiplayer/AI-ranking features.\n- Keep explanations technically precise, concise, and honest about what was tested programmatically vs. what requires manual live GPU browser inspection.\n</summary>"
