  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Pointer Lock**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating the Pointer Lock API into the `InputManager.ts` file, and utilizing the `{ unadjustedMovement: true }` option when available to address the critical mouse movement and continuous turning issues. This should give me the fine-grained control needed for a smoother experience.\n\n\n**Refining Pointer Lock Integration**\n\nI\'ve significantly refined the Pointer Lock implementation to address prior issues. Now, I directly read relative movement data from `e.movementX` and `e.movementY`, eliminating dependencies on absolute coordinates and cursor recentering. I\'m also addressing browser glitch spikes and fixed the fallback drag-on-unlocked-click bug. Additionally, I\'ve added an `F3` shortcut for toggling the Performance Monitor in dev mode. Finally, I\'ve cleaned up `FlightController.ts`.\n\n\n**Optimizing Angular Control**\n\nI\'ve resolved the reticle snap-back by removing the clamping and auto-recentering from the previous angular calculations. Now, relative deltas feed into a damped angular impulse for smooth, continuous rotation, completely unrestricted and with no gimbal lock or edge caps. This method gives micro-movement precision, while retaining thrust and boost physics. The reticle now aligns with ship forward.\n\n\n**Improving Reticle Accuracy**\n\nMy focus is now on the in-game boresight aiming reticle. I\'ve ensured a 1:1 correspondence with the target, eliminating any rubber-band snap-back. I\'ve also added `isPriorityTarget: false` to the initial enemy marker creation and initialized new Phase 3 performance telemetry fields to track various active game elements and asset loading. Simultaneously, I\'ve implemented a smooth third-person chase camera within `CameraController.ts`, allowing continuous 360\302\260+ movement without flipping or snapping. It incorporates subtle turn-rate lag.\n\n\n**Managing Asset Loading**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a robust asset-loading pipeline, including granular progress reporting and `AbortSignal` support. This handles PBR textures, mission-specific environments, and shared VFX. I\'m carefully managing asset lifetimes via reference counting with acquire/release. My goal is clean disposal of mission-specific textures during transitions while preserving necessary assets. This setup also accounts for error surfacing, load duration measurement, and robust cancelation.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "6gz_avChF4uUmtkPnfDimAE"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_9139495820861462271"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface InputSnapshot {\\n  forward: boolean;\\n  backward: boolean;\\n  rollLeft: boolean;\\n  rollRight: boolean;\\n  boost: boolean;\\n  firePrimary: boolean;\\n  keyPitchUp: boolean;\\n  keyPitchDown: boolean;\\n  keyYawLeft: boolean;\\n  keyYawRight: boolean;\\n  mouseDeltaX: number;\\n  mouseDeltaY: number;\\n  pointerLocked: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface InputCallbacks {\\n  onPauseRequested?: () => void;\\n  onPointerLockChanged?: (locked: boolean) => void;\\n  onToggleHudHints?: () => void;\\n  onTogglePerfMonitor?: () => void;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Decoupled keyboard + Pointer Lock mouse input manager.\\n *\\n * Continuous Mouse Turning Design (Phase 3 Fix):\\n * - Uses Pointer Lock API with pure relative `event.movementX` / `event.movementY`.\\n * - Never depends on absolute `clientX` / `clientY` coordinates or cursor recentering.\\n * - No artificial screen-boundary restriction or low delta clamping.\\n * - Preserves ESC pause behavior and cleanly re-engages Pointer Lock synchronously on user click.\\n */\\nexport class InputManager {\\n  private keys = new Set<string>();\\n  private mouseDeltaX = 0;\\n  private mouseDeltaY = 0;\\n  private pointerLocked = false;\\n  private mouseFireHeld = false;\\n  private lockTarget: HTMLElement | null = null;\\n  private active = false;\\n  private callbacks: InputCallbacks = {};\\n\\n  private readonly snapshot: InputSnapshot = {\\n    forward: false,\\n    backward: false,\\n    rollLeft: false,\\n    rollRight: false,\\n    boost: false,\\n    firePrimary: false,\\n    keyPitchUp: false,\\n    keyPitchDown: false,\\n    keyYawLeft: false,\\n    keyYawRight: false,\\n    mouseDeltaX: 0,\\n    mouseDeltaY: 0,\\n    pointerLocked: false,\\n  };\\n\\n  public attach(callbacks: InputCallbacks): void {\\n    this.callbacks = callbacks;\\n    window.addEventListener(\'keydown\', this.handleKeyDown);\\n    window.addEventListener(\'keyup\', this.handleKeyUp);\\n    window.addEventListener(\'mousemove\', this.handleMouseMove);\\n    window.addEventListener(\'mousedown\', this.handleMouseDown);\\n    window.addEventListener(\'mouseup\', this.handleMouseUp);\\n    window.addEventListener(\'blur\', this.handleBlur);\\n    document.addEventListener(\'pointerlockchange\', this.handlePointerLockChange);\\n    document.addEventListener(\'pointerlockerror\', this.handlePointerLockError);\\n  }\\n\\n  public detach(): void {\\n    window.removeEventListener(\'keydown\', this.handleKeyDown);\\n    window.removeEventListener(\'keyup\', this.handleKeyUp);\\n    window.removeEventListener(\'mousemove\', this.handleMouseMove);\\n    window.removeEventListener(\'mousedown\', this.handleMouseDown);\\n    window.removeEventListener(\'mouseup\', this.handleMouseUp);\\n    window.removeEventListener(\'blur\', this.handleBlur);\\n    document.removeEventListener(\'pointerlockchange\', this.handlePointerLockChange);\\n    document.removeEventListener(\'pointerlockerror\', this.handlePointerLockError);\\n    this.keys.clear();\\n    this.mouseFireHeld = false;\\n    this.resetDeltas();\\n  }\\n\\n  public setLockTarget(el: HTMLElement | null): void {\\n    this.lockTarget = el;\\n  }\\n\\n  public setActive(isActive: boolean): void {\\n    this.active = isActive;\\n    if (!isActive) {\\n      this.keys.clear();\\n      this.mouseFireHeld = false;\\n      this.resetDeltas();\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Synchronously requests Pointer Lock within a direct user gesture.\\n   * Attempts raw unadjusted movement first (eliminating OS pointer acceleration spikes)\\n   * and falls back seamlessly to standard Pointer Lock if unsupported.\\n   */\\n  public requestPointerLock(): void {\\n    const target = this.lockTarget ?? document.body;\\n    if (!target || typeof target.requestPointerLock !== \'function\') return;\\n    if (document.pointerLockElement === target) {\\n      this.pointerLocked = true;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const requestRaw = target.requestPointerLock as unknown as (\\n      options?: { unadjustedMovement?: boolean },\\n    ) => Promise<void> | void;\\n\\n    try {\\n      const maybePromise = requestRaw.call(target, { unadjustedMovement: true });\\n      if (maybePromise && typeof maybePromise.catch === \'function\') {\\n        maybePromise.catch(() => {\\n          try {\\n            const fallback = target.requestPointerLock() as unknown as Promise<void> | undefined;\\n            if (fallback && typeof fallback.catch === \'function\') {\\n              fallback.catch(() => {\\n                // Graceful fallback if browser/iframe temporarily blocks lock\\n              });\\n            }\\n          } catch {\\n            // Ignore sandboxed pointer lock exceptions\\n          }\\n        });\\n      }\\n    } catch {\\n      try {\\n        target.requestPointerLock();\\n      } catch {\\n        // Ignore sandboxed pointer lock exceptions\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  public exitPointerLock(): void {\\n    if (document.pointerLockElement && typeof document.exitPointerLock === \'function\') {\\n      try {\\n        document.exitPointerLock();\\n      } catch {\\n        // Ignore\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  public isPointerLocked(): boolean {\\n    return this.pointerLocked;\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Reads current key/button states and consumes accumulated relative mouse deltas for one frame.\\n   */\\n  public consumeSnapshot(): InputSnapshot {\\n    this.snapshot.forward = this.keys.has(\'KeyW\');\\n    this.snapshot.backward = this.keys.has(\'KeyS\');\\n    this.snapshot.rollLeft = this.keys.has(\'KeyA\');\\n    this.snapshot.rollRight = this.keys.has(\'KeyD\');\\n    this.snapshot.boost = this.keys.has(\'ShiftLeft\') || this.keys.has(\'ShiftRight\');\\n    this.snapshot.firePrimary = this.mouseFireHeld || this.keys.has(\'Space\');\\n    this.snapshot.keyPitchUp = this.keys.has(\'ArrowDown\');\\n    this.snapshot.keyPitchDown = this.keys.has(\'ArrowUp\');\\n    this.snapshot.keyYawLeft = this.keys.has(\'ArrowLeft\');\\n    this.snapshot.keyYawRight = this.keys.has(\'ArrowRight\');\\n    this.snapshot.mouseDeltaX = this.mouseDeltaX;\\n    this.snapshot.mouseDeltaY = this.mouseDeltaY;\\n    this.snapshot.pointerLocked = this.pointerLocked;\\n\\n    this.mouseDeltaX = 0;\\n    this.mouseDeltaY = 0;\\n    return this.snapshot;\\n  }\\n\\n  private resetDeltas(): void {\\n    this.mouseDeltaX = 0;\\n    this.mouseDeltaY = 0;\\n  }\\n\\n  private handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent): void => {\\n    if (e.code === \'Escape\') {\\n      if (this.active) {\\n        e.preventDefault();\\n        this.exitPointerLock();\\n        this.callbacks.onPauseRequested?.();\\n      }\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (e.code === \'KeyH\' && this.active && !e.repeat) {\\n      this.callbacks.onToggleHudHints?.();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (import.meta.env.DEV && e.code === \'F3\' && !e.repeat) {\\n      e.preventDefault();\\n      this.callbacks.onTogglePerfMonitor?.();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (!this.active) return;\\n\\n    if (\\n      e.code === \'KeyW\' ||\\n      e.code === \'KeyS\' ||\\n      e.code === \'KeyA\' ||\\n      e.code === \'KeyD\' ||\\n      e.code === \'ShiftLeft\' ||\\n      e.code === \'ShiftRight\' ||\\n      e.code === \'Space\' ||\\n      e.code === \'ArrowUp\' ||\\n      e.code === \'ArrowDown\' ||\\n      e.code === \'ArrowLeft\' ||\\n      e.code === \'ArrowRight\'\\n    ) {\\n      if (e.code === \'Space\') e.preventDefault();\\n      this.keys.add(e.code);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  private handleKeyUp = (e: KeyboardEvent): void => {\\n    this.keys.delete(e.code);\\n  };\\n\\n  private handleMouseMove = (e: MouseEvent): void => {\\n    if (!this.active || !this.pointerLocked) return;\\n\\n    // Pure relative hardware deltas from Pointer Lock API (zero screen-boundary restriction).\\n    // Guard only against extreme synthetic OS pointer-jump glitches (> 600px in a single event).\\n    const rawX = Number.isFinite(e.movementX) ? e.movementX : 0;\\n    const rawY = Number.isFinite(e.movementY) ? e.movementY : 0;\\n    if (Math.abs(rawX) > 600 || Math.abs(rawY) > 600) return;\\n\\n    this.mouseDeltaX += rawX;\\n    this.mouseDeltaY += rawY;\\n  };\\n\\n  private handleMouseDown = (e: MouseEvent): void => {\\n    if (!this.active || e.button !== 0) return;\\n\\n    if (this.pointerLocked) {\\n      this.mouseFireHeld = true;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Clicking the game viewport while unlocked re-engages Pointer Lock synchronously\\n    // without firing a stray weapon burst or relying on absolute cursor coordinates.\\n    if (e.target instanceof HTMLCanvasElement) {\\n      this.requestPointerLock();\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  private handleMouseUp = (e: MouseEvent): void => {\\n    if (e.button === 0) {\\n      this.mouseFireHeld = false;\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  private handleBlur = (): void => {\\n    this.keys.clear();\\n    this.mouseFireHeld = false;\\n    this.resetDeltas();\\n  };\\n\\n  private handlePointerLockChange = (): void => {\\n    const wasLocked = this.pointerLocked;\\n    this.pointerLocked = Boolean(document.pointerLockElement);\\n    this.mouseFireHeld = false;\\n    this.resetDeltas();\\n    this.callbacks.onPointerLockChanged?.(this.pointerLocked);\\n\\n    if (wasLocked && !this.pointerLocked && this.active) {\\n      this.callbacks.onPauseRequested?.();\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  private handlePointerLockError = (): void => {\\n    this.pointerLocked = false;\\n    this.callbacks.onPointerLockChanged?.(false);\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Fix InputManager to use pure relative Pointer Lock movementX/movementY with zero screen-edge restrictions or absolute cursor fallback\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/engine/InputManager.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Fixing InputManager continuous mouse turning\", \"toolSummary\":\"Fix InputManager mouse handling\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\243,\n\240,\001i\024}\023\312O\202\216\326\377\"1\331\211\225P\202q\222\034\035\017\370\204/N\030g\213\244$\260r\216e\275\274f\266\273L\035\336\234x\"H\aY\0326\177\232\316\353\323\251\346|\260\372\336\370pE\310\310\272\r\024\210\202\311a\361\274p-\322\002I\265\312$\313\352\354`9\270\037\301\326\035\001\223\273\\l\301\301\027\236f\033VA\250\r\027\345\314\030/d\242\313\234\374\"\370x\262\001\315\033=-J\310\t.\216\316\313t>\3502\212zP\030\325\212 \246\236\016Iq\326\3524\022\024n\344f_\254\363\324\303\207@j\314A\234\023\303{\221\365\303\t/(\245_Do\025\340xx\330\"y\337\227\315\321\307g\300C\350Xr\317\v\231\023\377\261\ag\262\030\302\v=,\004,\276=\337\300x\005QV\276o\357\246\364\316\024\244\300 ]H\3553\"\306\345\373G\311H\277v_\v\205\321\311g\350\017\000\227\201\200zD*J\211\264\263\257\303\351\205\004X\254\276\226\000v\236),\321Ts\324\304\260h\354p\217Ue9z\375o\331\373\271L\306\325&\260N\313\314\fG\210I&\356\343\205\355\351\036i\215\230N\310\345\265\375\244\243\356VXFw\347\315\031\266<\035\231\004C\324+:<\372\322\025\247\375\376\264\342|\262\352\327\210\203\313\036\302\n\35312\037\360\266\324Y\331\004f:@\275\031\002M\252\302Xv\230&\306\243\036\027\377\031\327Rv\257Rf|\305Z\335X\201\337\345_W?\353\212@AC8\251r\270\177\373tU6\216\220\374\311\025\235\242\277\240N#\306!\205\274\215\377\023\367\337p\340\357c\221\321>\340$\2664\033\205 %\2072\222[gD\t\204\304D\214\264\374\246\334\323\241\236\374\326\004_\374\001*O\023\352\211H\300\232z)\357\333F\375~Z\360zO7!\270\3574\346\223&hdz\017\251\215\303\\\374\260_X\247z\323B\375\036PB\250/<\202l\210\347\t9\',\3742\352s\037\337\3756\330\254\030\376\307R+\375\200:E\0301\202\227\307\nwnzTWD4U\243\035\361\001\022\261\253tKV\271J\034{pU\n/\374*\333\002%\266\222\213;+\264\026VY\265F/\253Y\'J\341\200\2529\bw\224\370\242sbk\200,?\251\325O\201\374\230M\333\346/T\312\310\026\247Xd\212\331\t\030\026\334_\302\364\227.\257\0267e85\366\314\262>\033!\254\342\020\276!\314>\372\241K{\250\203\253a\326\260L&\253\376x\025in