  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n# STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 3 Final Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Task Overview\nWe have completed **STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 3: Mission Campaign, Progressive Loading & Performance Engineering** for our browser-based 3D sci-fi arcade space combat game (React 19 + TypeScript + Three.js + React Three Fiber + Drei + Web Audio API).\n- **Phase 3 Deliverables (All Implemented & Verified)**:\n  1. Complete single-player 5-mission campaign (`MissionManager`, 4 objective types, progressive unlocks, `CampaignProgressStore`, deterministic `RankCalculator` S/A/B/C, `MissionSelectView`, `MissionResultsOverlay`, HUD Objectives & Announcements).\n  2. Critical continuous mouse movement & turning fix (`InputManager`, `FlightController`, `CameraController`, `FlightHUD`, `App.tsx`) eliminating screen-edge restrictions and cursor/reticle snap-back.\n  3. 5-stage progressive asset loading (`AssetManager` Stages A\342\200\223E with reference counting, caching, abort cancellation, error recovery, mission-scoped GPU disposal, and diagnostics).\n  4. Runtime performance engineering (distance-based enemy light/effect LOD culling, quality-scaled pooled particles & shockwaves, adaptive nebula shader FBM octaves, resolution/DPR scaling, Low/Medium/High/Ultra presets + working granular graphics settings, and dev-only Performance Monitor).\n- **Scope Boundaries Respected**:\n  - Did NOT implement full 3-ship unlock economy, LAN multiplayer, invitation codes, signaling, WebRTC, or room management.\n  - Preserved Phase 1/2 flight physics (`W/S` thrust, `A/D` roll, `Shift` boost), combat engine, and deep navy / electric cyan / dark metallic visual identity.\n- **ONLY REMAINING ACTION**: Deliver the final Phase 3 completion report directly to the user covering all **13 required reporting items** (no further code changes or tool calls needed unless the user requests follow-ups).\n\n## 2. Progress\n\n### Completed & Verified Files (Phase 3)\n**New files created in Phase 3:**\n- `/src/types/mission.ts` \342\200\224 Full mission campaign, difficulty profile, objective, wave, environment theme, scoring, result, persistence, and HUD snapshot contracts.\n- `/src/config/difficulty.ts` \342\200\224 5 difficulty profiles (`rookie`, `normal`, `veteran`, `expert`, `elite`) scaling reaction time, aim spread, agility, speed, fire cadence, evasion, squad coordination interval, and burst pressure.\n- `/src/config/missions.ts` \342\200\224 5 campaign missions (`mission-01` First Contact [Rookie, 2 enemies], `mission-02` Hostile Squadron [Normal, 4 enemies], `mission-03` Ambush [Veteran, 5 enemies, 20s survival + eliminate all], `mission-04` Ace Hunters [Expert, 3 elite enemies], `mission-05` Final Stand [Elite, 3 waves, 9 enemies total culminating in Ace boss `SOVEREIGN-ONE`]), each with its own `MissionEnvironmentTheme`.\n- `/src/engine/mission/RankCalculator.ts` \342\200\224 Deterministic 0\342\200\2231000 scoring (`Combat 400 + Accuracy 250 + Survival 200 + Speed 150`; `S >= 820`, `A >= 660`, `B >= 480`, `C < 480`) + `isBetterRank()`.\n- `/src/engine/mission/CampaignProgressStore.ts` \342\200\224 Safe LocalStorage persistence (`starfall.campaign.v1`) with schema version validation, corrupt-JSON fallback, `isMissionUnlocked()`, and `recordMissionOutcome()` preserving best rank/score/time.\n- `/src/engine/mission/MissionManager.ts` \342\200\224 Decoupled mission runtime driving waves, all 4 objective types (`eliminate_all`, `survive_duration`, `defeat_target`, `survive_waves`), tactical announcements, victory/failure evaluation, and discrete React callbacks (zero per-frame React renders).\n- `/src/components/MissionSelectView.tsx` \342\200\224 Campaign operations screen listing all 5 missions with mission number/code, difficulty, sector, enemy/wave count, objectives, lock/completion status, best rank/score/time, reward note, and Launch action.\n- `/src/components/MissionResultsOverlay.tsx` \342\200\224 Post-mission debrief showing Completed/Failed state, `S/A/B/C` rank, 4-category score breakdown bars, Enemies Defeated, Accuracy %, Time Taken, Damage Received, Hull %, Next Mission Unlock banner, and Next Mission / Retry / Mission Select / Main Menu actions.\n\n**Existing files updated in Phase 3:**\n- `/src/types/game.ts` \342\200\224 Added `\'results\'` phase, `\'missions\'` menu section, `\'ultra\'` graphics quality, `ShadowQuality`, `EffectQuality`, granular graphics fields in `GameSettings`, dev performance telemetry fields in `FlightTelemetry`, and error/mission fields in `LoadingProgress`.\n- `/src/types/combat.ts` \342\200\224 Added `difficultyLevel`, `isPriorityTarget`, `coordinationTimer` to `EnemyEntity`; `callsign` and `isPriorityTarget` to `DestructionEvent`; `isPriorityTarget` to `ProjectedEnemyMarker`.\n- `/src/config/graphics.ts` \342\200\224 Full `low | medium | high | ultra` presets + `getGraphicsPresetPatch()` + `resolveEffectiveGraphics(settings)` applying granular `resolutionScale`, `shadowQuality`, `particleQuality`, `environmentDetail`, `drawDistance`, `antialias`, and `postGlowEnabled`.\n- `/src/config/ships.ts` \342\200\224 Updated `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` and `loadSavedSettings()` (`starfall.settings.v2` with backward-compatible fallback to `v1` and dev-only gating of `showPerfOverlay`).\n- `/src/config/botPersonalities.ts` \342\200\224 Connected `resolveBotDifficultyTuning()` directly to `DIFFICULTY_PROFILES`.\n- `/src/engine/combat/EnemyAIController.ts` \342\200\224 Uses `DifficultyProfile` tuning for reaction time, spread, agility, speed, fire cadence, evasion, squad coordination flank-flip intervals (`coordinationTimer`), and burst pressure scaling (`burstPressureScale`).\n- `/src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts` \342\200\224 Added `missionMode`, `clearCombatState()`, `spawnMissionWave()`, `getActiveEnemyCount()`, `getActiveProjectileCount()`, `isPriorityTarget` marker propagation, and telemetry counts (`activeEnemies`, `activeProjectiles`).\n- `/src/engine/InputManager.ts` \342\200\224 Fixed mouse control: pure Pointer Lock relative `e.movementX`/`e.movementY` with `{ unadjustedMovement: true }` + fallback, zero absolute `clientX/clientY` dependency, no low delta clamp (only `> 600px` OS glitch guard), synchronous `requestPointerLock()` on canvas click without firing a stray shot, preserved `ESC` pause, and dev-only `F3` perf monitor toggle.\n- `/src/engine/FlightController.ts` \342\200\224 Removed clamped gimbal aim box (`MAX_AIM_YAW_RAD = 23\302\260`, `MAX_AIM_PITCH_RAD = 17\302\260`) and auto-recentering pullback (`aimYawOffset -= stepYaw`); replaced with unbounded continuous relative-delta quaternion turning (`pendingYawRad`/`pendingPitchRad` critically damped at `24/s`) preserving fine micro-precision (`<= 5px`) and unlimited 360\302\260+ turns with zero snap-back; thrust/boost/roll unchanged.\n- `/src/engine/CameraController.ts` \342\200\224 Refined orthonormalized up-vector tracking and direct forward look target for smooth 360\302\260+ continuous turns and loops.\n- `/src/engine/AssetManager.ts` \342\200\224 Upgraded to 5-stage progressive loader (Stage A Boot shared glow only; Stage B Hangar idle ship preloading; Stage C async `loadMissionAssets` with mission-themed planet/moon/asteroid textures, hull PBR maps, `AbortSignal`, progress callback, duration tracking, and error recovery; Stage D ref-counted runtime cache; Stage E `releaseMissionSession` disposing mission-scoped GPU textures while keeping shared resources intact) + `getDiagnostics()`.\n- `/src/scene/shipGeometry.ts` \342\200\224 Uses ref-counted `AssetManager.acquireHullTextures` / `acquireGlowSprite` with matching releases in `dispose()`, plus `setDetailLevel(highDetail)` for distance LOD culling of engine `PointLight` and glow sprites.\n- `/src/scene/SpaceEnvironment.tsx` \342\200\224 Supports per-mission `MissionEnvironmentTheme` palettes, ref-counted mission environment textures, adaptive nebula shader FBM octaves (`uOctaves`), shadow map size scaling, asteroid/star/planet segment scaling, and atmosphere glow toggle.\n- `/src/scene/EnemyShipRenderer.tsx` \342\200\224 Distance-based LOD culling toggling enemy engine `PointLight` and hit/engine sprites beyond `graphics.enemyLightLodDistance`.\n- `/src/scene/CombatVFX.tsx` \342\200\224 Quality-scaled particle/shockwave pool caps & spark counts, ref-counted `glowSprite`, and live `telemetryRef.current.activeParticles` reporting.\n- `/src/scene/GameScene.tsx` & `/src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx` \342\200\224 Wired `MissionManager`, `missionTheme`, DPR resolution scaling, and 250ms asset/render telemetry updates.\n- `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx` \342\200\224 Added Mission Objectives panel, non-blocking tactical announcement banner, priority boss diamond highlight (`\342\230\205 SOVEREIGN-ONE`), removed rubber-band tether line for clean 1:1 boresight reticle, and gated extended Performance Monitor strictly behind `import.meta.env.DEV && settings.showPerfOverlay`.\n- `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx` \342\200\224 Low/Medium/High/Ultra presets + granular Resolution Scale, Shadow Quality, Particle & VFX Quality, Environment Detail, Draw Distance, Anti-Aliasing, Atmosphere Glow, and dev-only Performance Monitor (`F3`) toggle.\n- `/src/components/LoadingScreen.tsx` \342\200\224 Shows mission code/name/sector, progress bar, Cancel button, and structured Error Recovery UI (Retry Load / Mission Select).\n- `/src/components/MainMenu.tsx` & `/src/components/PauseOverlay.tsx` & `/src/App.tsx` \342\200\224 Complete campaign navigation, Stage B idle Hangar preloading, Stage C mission loading/abort/retry, Stage E cleanup on exit, synchronous Pointer Lock restoration, and mission results integration.\n\n### Verification Commands Executed & Exact Results\n1. `compile_applet` (Vite production build): **PASSED** (`Build succeeded - the applet is compiled`).\n2. `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`): **PASSED** (0 TypeScript errors).\n3. `restart_dev_server` + `curl http://localhost:3000/`: **PASSED** (`DEV_SERVER_HTTP=200`).\n4. Comprehensive 8-part automated `npx tsx` test & benchmark suite: **ALL 8 PASSED (exit code 0)**:\n   - `[1/8] Continuous Mouse Turning`: 180-frame continuous sweep achieved **848.3\302\260** uninterrupted rotation (zero clamp/stall), micro 2px input produced **0.226\302\260** precision turn, idle drift after stopping mouse = **0.0000\302\260** (zero snap-back), boost speed & drain verified.\n   - `[2/8] All 5 Campaign Missions`: Verified exact enemy counts (`2, 4, 5, 3, 9`), Mission 03 combined `survive_duration` (20s) + `eliminate_all` (5), Mission 05 3-wave progression + priority Ace `SOVEREIGN-ONE` (`defeat_target` + `survive_waves`), and player destruction failure state (`rank: null`).\n   - `[3/8] Difficulty Scaling`: Monotonic scaling verified across `rookie -> normal -> veteran -> expert -> elite` for reaction time, aim spread, turn rate, fire cadence, and squad coordination interval.\n   - `[4/8] Deterministic RankCalculator`: Strictly repeatable identical outputs; verified thresholds `S=991`, `A=800`, `B=564`, `C=219`.\n   - `[5/8] Campaign Progression Store`: Unlock chain `M01 -> M02 -> M03 -> M04 -> M05`, best rank/score preservation on lower-rank replays, and schema-safe `loadCampaignProgress()`.\n   - `[6/8] Progressive AssetManager (Stages A\342\200\223E)`: Verified Stage A shared sprite, Stage C mission load caching, Stage E disposal of mission env textures while preserving referenced shared sprite, simulated load error rejection, and `AbortController` cancellation without ref leaks.\n   - `[7/8] Adaptive Graphics Presets`: Verified `low < medium < high < ultra` scaling plus granular overrides (`resolutionScale: 0.7`, `shadowQuality: \'off\'`, `drawDistance: 2200`).\n   - `[8/8] High-Intensity Simulation Benchmark (2,000 frames @ 60Hz, 5 active AI bots + continuous firing + swept collisions + camera projection + mission update)`: **avg = 0.214 ms**, **p95 = 0.326 ms**, **p99 = 0.620 ms** (CPU simulation cost in Node v22; well under 16.67 ms 60 FPS budget).\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Mouse Turning Root Cause (Section 2)**:\n  1. In Phase 2, `App.tsx` called `requestPointerLock()` asynchronously *after* `await AssetManager.prepareFlightSession()`, breaking the browser\'s synchronous user-gesture requirement so Pointer Lock failed silently and fell back to absolute `clientX`/`clientY` dragging (hitting screen edges).\n  2. `FlightController.ts` clamped `aimYawOffset`/`aimPitchOffset` to an ellipse (`23\302\260 \303\227 17\302\260`) and continuously subtracted ship rotation back toward center (`aimYawOffset -= stepYaw`), creating the visible snap-back and interrupting continuous turns.\n  - **Fix**: Removed clamped gimbal offsets and auto-recenter pullback completely; switched `FlightController` to unbounded continuous relative-delta quaternion integration (`pendingYawRad`/`pendingPitchRad`); updated `InputManager` to rely exclusively on Pointer Lock `e.movementX`/`e.movementY` (`unadjustedMovement: true` with fallback) with synchronous lock re-engagement on click/resume and no stray shot on lock click.\n- **Sandbox GPU Testing Boundary**: No headless Chromium/Playwright binary is installed in this sandbox environment. Automated verification covered TypeScript, Vite bundling, HTTP serving, flight/mouse math, missions, AI scaling, ranking, persistence, asset ref-counting/disposal, graphics config resolution, and CPU simulation frame times. Live browser GPU FPS/draw-call/Pointer-Lock UX validation must be honestly reported as not yet verified in a live GPU browser session.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- `tsc --noEmit` initially failed with 2 errors in `/src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts` (`Property \'activeCount\' is private and only accessible within class \'ProjectilePool\'`). Fixed by calling the existing public `this.projectiles.getActiveCount()` method. Re-ran `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` \342\200\224 both succeeded with 0 errors.\n- Also moved mid-file imports in `/src/config/botPersonalities.ts` to the top of the file to adhere strictly to top-level import guidelines.\n- No unresolved errors remain.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Codebase is completely clean, compiled, typechecked, and running cleanly on dev server port 3000 (`HTTP 200`).\n- No temporary test files were created on disk (tests ran inline via `npx tsx -e`).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Immediately output the concise, technically precise Phase 3 final report** directly to the user (no additional tool calls needed!) covering all **13 explicitly requested sections**:\n   1. Mission system architecture\n   2. Five missions implemented\n   3. Objective and progression systems\n   4. Rank calculation rules\n   5. Mouse movement root cause and exact fix\n   6. Asset Manager improvements\n   7. Progressive loading behavior (Stages A\342\200\223E)\n   8. Optimization techniques implemented\n   9. Graphics settings implemented\n   10. Performance measurements (honestly distinguish automated CPU simulation benchmark `avg 0.214ms / p95 0.326ms / p99 0.620ms` from live GPU browser FPS which requires manual browser inspection)\n   11. Tests performed (list exact commands/checks run and exact outcomes; explicitly state what was NOT tested in a live GPU browser)\n   12. Remaining issues / limitations (e.g., live browser WebGL GPU profiling, Pointer Lock behavior in sandboxed iframes, single playable ship VX-9 until Phase 4)\n   13. Recommended next development phase (Phase 4: Multi-Ship Unlocks & Progression \342\200\224 Striker & Destroyer playable chassis, secondary weapons/loadouts, and live GPU browser profiling pass before multiplayer).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow STARFALL Permanent Project Instructions & Phase 3 reporting checklist strictly.\n- Never claim live browser GPU FPS or manual interactive gameplay was tested when only automated verification and server/build checks were executed.\n- Keep explanations concise, technically precise, and scannable (avoid hype or fluff).\n</summary>"
