  planner_response {
    response: "# STARFALL \342\200\224 Phase 3 Completion Report\n\nPhase 3 (**Mission Campaign, Progressive Loading & Performance Engineering**) is implemented, type-checked, built, and verified against automated simulation and subsystem tests.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Mission System Architecture\n- **Decoupled Runtime**: `MissionManager` executes inside the existing frame loop (`GameScene`) using delta time, driving waves, objective evaluation, tactical announcements, and victory/failure transitions without per-frame React state updates.\n- **Discrete UI Callbacks**: React receives updates only on discrete events (wave transitions, objective state changes, announcements, and mission completion/failure).\n- **Combat Integration**: `CombatManager` supports `missionMode` with wave spawning (`spawnMissionWave`), priority target tracking (`isPriorityTarget`), state cleanup (`clearCombatState`), and active entity/projectile counters.\n- **Difficulty Profiles**: `DIFFICULTY_PROFILES` (`rookie`, `normal`, `veteran`, `expert`, `elite`) feed `EnemyAIController` via `resolveBotDifficultyTuning()` to scale reaction time, aim spread, turn agility, flight speed, fire cadence, evasion, squad flank-coordination intervals (`coordinationTimer`), and burst pressure (`burstPressureScale`).\n\n## 2. Five Missions Implemented\n| # | Mission | Difficulty | Enemies / Waves | Objectives | Environment Theme |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | **First Contact** | Rookie | 2 enemies (1 wave) | Eliminate all hostiles | Deep navy patrol sector |\n| 02 | **Hostile Squadron** | Normal | 4 enemies (1 wave) | Eliminate all hostiles | Cobalt orbital belt |\n| 03 | **Ambush** | Veteran | 5 enemies (1 wave) | Survive 20s ambush + Eliminate all hostiles | Amber-tinted hazard field |\n| 04 | **Ace Hunters** | Expert | 3 elite enemies (1 wave) | Eliminate all elite interceptors | High-contrast violet nebula |\n| 05 | **Final Stand** | Elite | 9 enemies (3 waves) | Survive all waves + Defeat priority Ace (`SOVEREIGN-ONE`) | Crimson/cyan deep-space core |\n\n## 3. Objective & Progression Systems\n- **Objective Types**: `eliminate_all`, `survive_duration`, `defeat_target`, and `survive_waves` are tracked live in the HUD Objectives panel with non-blocking tactical banners and diamond boss markers (`\342\230\205 SOVEREIGN-ONE`).\n- **Progression & Unlocks**: Completing Mission `N` unlocks Mission `N + 1` sequentially (`M01 -> M02 -> M03 -> M04 -> M05`).\n- **Persistence (`CampaignProgressStore`)**: Stored in `localStorage` under `starfall.campaign.v1` with schema version validation and corrupt-JSON fallback. Replaying a mission preserves the player\'s best rank, best score, and fastest clear time.\n- **Campaign UI**: Added `MissionSelectView` (lock/completion status, sector info, objectives, best records, launch) and `MissionResultsOverlay` (Completed/Failed state, rank badge, 4-category score breakdown, stats, unlock banner, and Next/Retry/Mission Select/Main Menu actions).\n\n## 4. Rank Calculation Rules\n`RankCalculator` computes a deterministic **0\342\200\2231000** score on mission completion (failed missions return `rank: null`):\n- **Combat** (up to **400 pts**): Enemies defeated and priority target completion.\n- **Accuracy** (up to **250 pts**): Shots hit vs. shots fired ratio.\n- **Survival** (up to **200 pts**): Remaining hull integrity and damage received.\n- **Speed** (up to **150 pts**): Clear time relative to mission par time.\n- **Rank Thresholds**: `S >= 820` \302\267 `A >= 660` \302\267 `B >= 480` \302\267 `C < 480`.\n\n## 5. Mouse Movement Root Cause & Exact Fix\n### Root Cause\n1. **Broken Pointer Lock Gesture**: `requestPointerLock()` was previously invoked *after* an `await` during session startup, violating browsers\' synchronous user-gesture requirement. Pointer Lock silently failed and fell back to absolute `clientX`/`clientY` tracking, hitting physical screen boundaries.\n2. **Clamped Gimbal Box & Snap-Back**: `FlightController` clamped aim offsets inside a `23\302\260 \303\227 17\302\260` ellipse (`MAX_AIM_YAW_RAD`, `MAX_AIM_PITCH_RAD`) and continuously subtracted ship turn deltas (`aimYawOffset -= stepYaw`), pulling the aim vector back toward center and interrupting sustained turns.\n\n### Fix Implemented\n- **`InputManager`**: Uses Pointer Lock relative deltas (`e.movementX` / `e.movementY`) with `{ unadjustedMovement: true }` (with standard fallback), removes absolute cursor fallback and low-delta clamping (retaining only a `> 600px` OS glitch guard), engages Pointer Lock synchronously on canvas click/resume without firing a stray shot, and preserves `ESC` pause handling.\n- **`FlightController` & `CameraController`**: Replaced the clamped gimbal offsets and auto-recenter pullback with unbounded relative-delta quaternion turning (`pendingYawRad` / `pendingPitchRad`, critically damped at `24/s`) and orthonormalized camera up-vector tracking for uninterrupted 360\302\260+ turns while preserving small-movement (`<= 5px`) precision and existing thrust/boost/roll physics.\n- **`FlightHUD`**: Removed the rubber-band tether line for a clean 1:1 boresight reticle.\n\n## 6. Asset Manager Improvements\n- Centralized reference counting (`acquire` / `release`) for shared glow sprites, ship hull PBR maps, and mission-scoped environment textures.\n- Cache reuse across retries/replays to avoid redundant procedural texture regeneration.\n- Mission load cancellation via `AbortSignal`, progress reporting, load-duration tracking, structured error recovery UI in `LoadingScreen` (Retry Load / Mission Select), and runtime diagnostics (`getDiagnostics()`).\n\n## 7. Progressive Loading Behavior (Stages A\342\200\223E)\n- **Stage A (Boot)**: Initializes only lightweight shared resources (glow sprite); no full mission or ship textures loaded at startup.\n- **Stage B (Hangar / Menu Idle)**: Background preloads player hull textures when viewing menus/hangar.\n- **Stage C (Mission Load)**: Asynchronously generates/loads mission-themed planet, moon, and asteroid textures plus required ship PBR maps with progress updates and abort support.\n- **Stage D (Active Gameplay)**: Runtime entities (`shipGeometry`, `SpaceEnvironment`, `CombatVFX`) acquire cached ref-counted handles with zero runtime texture allocations.\n- **Stage E (Exit / Cleanup)**: `releaseMissionSession()` disposes mission-scoped GPU textures while keeping still-referenced shared assets intact.\n\n## 8. Optimization Techniques Implemented\n- **Distance-Based LOD Culling**: `EnemyShipRenderer` and `shipGeometry.setDetailLevel()` disable enemy engine `PointLight` instances and secondary glow/hit sprites beyond `enemyLightLodDistance`.\n- **Quality-Scaled Pooling**: `CombatVFX` scales particle pool capacity, shockwave pools, and spark emission counts by active particle quality without per-frame allocations.\n- **Adaptive Shaders & Geometry**: `SpaceEnvironment` adjusts nebula shader FBM octaves (`uOctaves`), starfield/asteroid counts, planet mesh segments, and directional shadow map resolution based on effective graphics config.\n- **Resolution Scaling**: Dynamic canvas DPR clamping via `resolutionScale`.\n- **Dev-Only Performance Monitor**: Gated strictly behind `import.meta.env.DEV && settings.showPerfOverlay` (toggleable via `F3` or Settings in dev; hidden in production builds).\n\n## 9. Graphics Settings Implemented\n- **Presets**: `Low`, `Medium`, `High`, and `Ultra` via `getGraphicsPresetPatch()`.\n- **Granular Controls (`resolveEffectiveGraphics`)**:\n  - Resolution Scale (`0.5`\342\200\223`1.25`)\n  - Shadow Quality (`off`, `low`, `medium`, `high`)\n  - Particle & VFX Quality (`low`, `medium`, `high`, `ultra`)\n  - Environment Detail (`low`, `medium`, `high`, `ultra`)\n  - Draw Distance\n  - Anti-Aliasing toggle\n  - Atmosphere Glow toggle\n  - Dev-only Performance Monitor toggle (`F3`)\n- **Persistence**: Saved under `starfall.settings.v2` with backward-compatible fallback from `v1`.\n\n## 10. Performance Measurements\n- **Automated CPU Simulation Benchmark** (Node v22, `npx tsx`, 2,000 frames @ 60Hz with 5 active AI bots, continuous firing, swept hit detection, camera projection, and `MissionManager` updates):\n  - **Average frame simulation time**: `0.214 ms`\n  - **p95**: `0.326 ms`\n  - **p99**: `0.620 ms` (well within the `16.67 ms` 60 FPS frame budget)\n- **Live Browser GPU Metrics**: Not yet measured in this sandbox (no headless GPU browser/Playwright runtime available). Live WebGL FPS, draw calls, shader compile times, and GPU memory usage require verification in a desktop browser using the dev `F3` Performance Monitor.\n\n## 11. Tests Performed\n| Check | Outcome | Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| Production Build (`vite build`) | **Passed** | Clean bundle with 0 build errors. |\n| TypeScript Check (`tsc --noEmit`) | **Passed** | 0 type errors after fixing `ProjectilePool.getActiveCount()` accessor and top-level imports. |\n| Dev Server (`http://localhost:3000/`) | **Passed** | Responded `HTTP 200`. |\n| Automated 8-Part Subsystem Suite (`npx tsx`) | **8 / 8 Passed** | Verified: (1) 180-frame continuous mouse sweep (`848.3\302\260`, `0.226\302\260` micro-input, `0.0000\302\260` idle drift); (2) all 5 missions\' waves, objectives, boss kill, and failure state; (3) monotonic difficulty scaling across all 5 tiers; (4) deterministic `S/A/B/C` ranking (`991/800/564/219`); (5) unlock chain & best-record persistence; (6) AssetManager Stages A\342\200\223E caching, disposal, error rejection, and `AbortSignal` cancellation; (7) graphics preset & granular override resolution; (8) 2,000-frame combat/AI CPU benchmark. |\n\n**Not Tested**: Interactive browser playthrough, live WebGL GPU FPS across `Low`\342\200\223`Ultra` presets, Web Audio playback, and real OS Pointer Lock feel inside an embedded iframe.\n\n## 12. Remaining Issues & Limitations\n- **Live GPU Profiling Needed**: Shader octave cost, shadow map cost, and DPR scaling impacts have not yet been profiled on real GPU hardware in-browser.\n- **Sandboxed Iframe Pointer Lock**: Some browser/iframe policies restrict `unadjustedMovement` or require explicit user click after focus changes; fallback handling is in place, but manual verification in the target preview iframe is recommended.\n- **Single Playable Ship**: Only the **VX-9 Interceptor** is currently playable; Striker and Destroyer chassis and unlock economy remain scheduled for the next phase.\n\n## 13. Recommended Next Development Phase\n**Phase 4 \342\200\224 Multi-Ship Hangar, Unlocks & Combat Depth**:\n1. Implement the **Striker** and **Destroyer** playable spaceships with distinct 3D procedural geometry, flight handling envelopes, hull/shield ratings, and weapon profiles.\n2. Connect campaign rank/mission milestones to ship unlock progression in `CampaignProgressStore` and add an interactive 3D ship selector in the Hangar.\n3. Introduce secondary weapons/countermeasures (e.g., lock-on missiles or flak burst) and perform a live browser GPU & Pointer Lock profiling pass prior to starting Phase 5 multiplayer networking."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Compaction Summary**\n\nI\'m carefully examining the compaction summary now. Phase 3 for STARFALL is done: implementation, compilation (passed `compile_applet`), linting (passed `lint_applet`), dev server restart, and verification of `HTTP` are all complete.\n\n\n"
