**Automated CPU Simulation Benchmark** (Node v22, `npx tsx`, 2,000 frames @ 60Hz with 5 active AI bots, continuous firing, swept hit detection, camera projection, and `MissionManager` updates):\n  - **Average frame simulation time**: `0.214 ms`\n  - **p95**: `0.326 ms`\n  - **p99**: `0.620 ms` (well within the `16.67 ms` 60 FPS frame budget)\n- **Live Browser GPU Metrics**: Not yet measured in this sandbox (no headless GPU browser/Playwright runtime available). Live WebGL FPS, draw calls, shader compile times, and GPU memory usage require verification in a desktop browser using the dev `F3` Performance Monitor.\n\n## 11. Tests Performed\n| Check | Outcome | Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| Production Build (`vite build`) | **Passed** | Clean bundle with 0 build errors. |\n| TypeScript Check (`tsc --noEmit`) | **Passed** | 0 type errors after fixing `ProjectilePool.getActiveCount()` accessor and top-level imports. |\n| Dev Server (`http://localhost:3000/`) | **Passed** | Responded `HTTP 200`. |\n| Automated 8-Part Subsystem Suite (`npx tsx`) | **8 / 8 Passed** | Verified: (1) 180-frame continuous mouse sweep (`848.3\302\260`, `0.226\302\260` micro-input, `0.0000\302\260` idle drift); (2) all 5 missions\' waves, objectives, boss kill, and failure state; (3) monotonic difficulty scaling across all 5 tiers; (4) deterministic `S/A/B/C` ranking (`991/800/564/219`); (5) unlock chain & best-record persistence; (6) AssetManager Stages A\342\200\223E caching, disposal, error rejection, and `AbortSignal` cancellation; (7) graphics preset & granular override resolution; (8) 2,000-frame combat/AI CPU benchmark. |\n\n**Not Tested**: Interactive browser playthrough, live WebGL GPU FPS across `Low`\342\200\223`Ultra` presets, Web Audio playback, and real OS Pointer Lock feel inside an embedded iframe.\n\n## 12. Remaining Issues & Limitations\n- **Live GPU Profiling Needed**: Shader octave cost, shadow map cost, and DPR scaling impacts have not yet been profiled on real GPU hardware in-b