  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Unveiling a Solution**\n\nI\'ve hit a potential breakthrough! I observed that waiting for an element to be fully visible and enabled in R3F, especially when using SwiftShader, is causing slowdowns. But I\'ve noted that `page.locator(...).click({ force: true })` and `evaluate(el => el.click())` can bypass Playwright\'s stability checks while WebGL is drawing, which may be beneficial. Now I am using this!\n\n\n"
