  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Pinpointing the Cause**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `InputManager.ts` file, specifically the `handleKeyDown` function, and found a significant clue around line 129. I\'m seeing that `pausedCount` has a value of 2, instead of 1, where it shouldn\'t. I\'m going to investigate what is causing `pausedCount` to be incremented a second time, when I expect it to only increment once.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Double Trigger**\n\nI\'ve traced the double pause request. It seems the `pointerlockchange` event, triggered by `exitPointerLock`, fires a pause *before* React updates, leading to a redundant call in `handleKeyDown`. I can see two calls to `onPauseRequested`: one directly from `handleKeyDown` and another from `handlePointerLockChange`. The `phaseRef.current` condition in `App.tsx` failed to prevent this because the pointer lock event could fire *before* React state updated, allowing both pause calls to execute, triggering the audio *twice*. I need to adjust `handleKeyDown` to prevent the duplicated trigger. I could either check `isLockOwned()` or set `active = false`.\n\n\n**Refining the Logic**\n\nI\'ve been refining the logic, focusing on the asynchronous nature of `pointerlockchange` events. I\'m exploring conditions within the `handleKeyDown` function, particularly the interplay between `exitPointerLock` and the `pointerlockchange` event. I think I\'ve found a robust solution by conditionally calling `onPauseRequested` based on whether the lock was previously owned, or whether `this.active` has already been handled by a synchronous `pointerlockchange` call. This should prevent the double trigger elegantly and efficiently.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "_BH_atzqBJrQz7IPt7bL2Qc"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_881955066069251420"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Ensure Escape key triggers onPauseRequested exactly once regardless of whether pointerlockchange fires synchronously or asynchronously\", \"EndLine\":255, \"Instruction\":\"Update Escape handling in InputManager.ts handleKeyDown so onPauseRequested is only invoked if this.active is still true after exitPointerLock()\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  private handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent): void => {\\n    if (e.code === \'Escape\') {\\n      if (this.active) {\\n        e.preventDefault();\\n        this.exitPointerLock();\\n        if (this.active) {\\n          this.callbacks.onPauseRequested?.();\\n        }\\n      }\\n      return;\\n    }\", \"StartLine\":238, \"TargetContent\":\"  private handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent): void => {\\n    if (e.code === \'Escape\') {\\n      if (this.active) {\\n        e.preventDefault();\\n        this.exitPointerLock();\\n        this.callbacks.onPauseRequested?.();\\n      }\\n      return;\\n    }\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/engine/InputManager.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Fixing Escape pause deduplication in InputManager.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Fix Escape pause count\"}"
