  planner_response {
    response: "# STARFALL \342\200\224 Mouse Boundary Rollback Fix Report\n\n## 1. Exact Root Cause\nInspection of the live Chromium Pointer Lock lifecycle and input pipeline revealed three interacting causes of boundary rollback and Pointer Lock instability:\n\n1. **Chromium/OS Boundary Cursor-Warp Rollback Spikes (`movementX` / `movementY`)**:\n   - Even while `document.pointerLockElement === canvas` is active, Chromium\'s non-raw Pointer Lock implementation (in iframes, macOS, Linux/Wayland/X11, scaled viewports, and virtualized displays) warps the hidden cursor back toward the lock center when it reaches a screen or iframe edge, emitting an opposite-direction `mousemove` spike equal to `center - edge` (e.g., `-250px` to `-550px` in preview panes).\n   - `InputManager.handleMouseMove` previously only dropped deltas `> 600px`, allowing every viewport/iframe edge warp jump (`<= 600px`) straight into `FlightController`, instantly snapping/rolling the ship and camera backward.\n\n2. **`unadjustedMovement: true` Async Rejection & `pointerlockerror` Loop**:\n   - Live Chromium testing showed `canvas.requestPointerLock({ unadjustedMovement: true })` immediately rejected with `NotSupportedError` and fired a `pointerlockerror` event, forcing an asynchronous fallback call inside `.catch()` (outside the synchronous user-gesture stack) and transiently resetting `pointerLocked` state.\n\n3. **Duplicate `mousedown` / Pointer Lock Listeners & Missing Target Ownership Verification**:\n   - `FlightCanvas` (`div` `onMouseDown`) and `InputManager` (`window` `mousedown`) both invoked `requestPointerLock()` on the same click.\n   - `InputManager` lacked an attachment guard against duplicate listener registration, checked `Boolean(document.pointerLockElement)` rather than verifying `document.pointerLockElement === this.lockTarget`, and could invoke `onPauseRequested` twice when pressing `Escape`.\n\n*(Verified clean: `FlightController`, `CameraController`, and `CombatManager` use unbounded local-space quaternion turning and 3D world-space camera tracking with no cursor recentering or screen-edge clamping.)*\n\n---\n\n## 2. Relevant Code Locations\n- `src/engine/InputManager.ts`\n- `src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx`\n- `src/App.tsx`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exact Fix Applied\n- **`src/engine/InputManager.ts`**:\n  - **Synchronous Standard Pointer Lock**: Removed `{ unadjustedMovement: true }` so `requestPointerLock()` runs synchronously on `this.lockTarget` without `NotSupportedError` rejections or spurious `pointerlockerror` events.\n  - **Strict Ownership Verification (`isLockOwned`)**: Verifies `document.pointerLockElement === this.lockTarget` in `pointerlockchange`, `pointerlockerror`, `handleMouseMove`, `handleMouseDown`, and `consumeSnapshot()`.\n  - **Boundary Cursor-Warp Rollback Filtering (`isAnomalousWarpJump`)**: Filters anomalous single-event warp spikes (`|raw| > 350` or sudden opposite-sign jumps `>= 90px` exceeding `3.2x` recent sustained directional movement) while passing 100% of fine micro-movements (`1\342\200\2235px`), continuous sweeps, and smooth human direction reversals without clamping or recentering.\n  - **Single-Listener Lifecycle & Pause Deduplication**: Guarded `attach()` against duplicate listener registration, ensured `detach()` removes all listeners and exits owned Pointer Lock on unmount, and deduplicated `Escape` pause invocation across synchronous/asynchronous `pointerlockchange` timing.\n- **`src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx` & `src/App.tsx`**:\n  - Removed the duplicate `onMouseDown` wrapper handler and `onCanvasClick` prop so `InputManager` is the sole owner of canvas mouse & Pointer Lock input.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Pointer-Lock & Build Verification\n- **Production Build (`vite build`) & Type Check (`tsc --noEmit`)**: Both passed with 0 errors.\n- **Unit & Simulation Verification (`npx tsx`)**:\n  - Verified duplicate `attach()` prevention and full listener removal + lock release on `detach()`.\n  - Verified non-canvas `pointerLockElement` rejection (`isPointerLocked() === false`).\n  - Verified continuous 120-frame rightward turning (`231.9\302\260` total rotation) with injected `-420px` and `-260px` edge warp spikes cleanly filtered (`warpSpikesFiltered: 2`), `0.254\302\260` fine micro-precision (`2px` input), intact human smooth reversals, and single-fire `Escape` pause.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Actual Browser Test Results (Headless Chromium via Playwright)\nExecuted live end-to-end tests in Chromium (`1280\303\227720` top-level and `1024\303\227640` `<iframe>` with `allow=\"pointer-lock\"`):\n1. **Pointer Lock Engagement**: Entered gameplay (`M-01`) -> `document.pointerLockElement === \"CANVAS\"`, **`0` `pointerlockerror` events**, and the engage prompt remained hidden.\n2. **Iframe Support**: Verified `document.pointerLockElement === \"CANVAS\"` inside a `1024\303\227640` embedded `<iframe>`.\n3. **Continuous Mouse Turning & Edge Warp Suppression**: Dispatched continuous relative `mousemove` sweeps (`movementX: +20`, `movementY: -12`, fine `+2px`) alongside a simulated `-420px` edge-warp spike -> HUD attitude advanced smoothly from `HDG 000\302\260 / PITCH +0\302\260` to `HDG 047\302\260` and `HDG 050\302\260 / PITCH +15\302\260` with zero rollback.\n4. **Keyboard Flight Controls**: `W + Shift + A` accelerated to `42 m/s` (`BOOSTING`) and rolled to `ROLL +15\302\260` as expected.\n5. **ESC Release & Resume**: `Escape` released Pointer Lock (`document.pointerLockElement === null`) and opened `Flight Paused`; clicking `Resume Flight` re-locked `\"CANVAS\"` with `0` errors.\n\n*Note*: Automated browser verification ran in headless Chromium (SwiftShader) using DOM/Playwright events; a final manual check with a physical desktop mouse in your target preview browser is recommended to confirm OS-level hardware feel."
    message_id: "exL_auX3OdeRmtkP-7Op4Ac"
    modified_response: "# STARFALL \342\200\224 Mouse Boundary Rollback Fix Report\n\n## 1. Exact Root Cause\nInspection of the live Chromium Pointer Lock lifecycle and input pipeline revealed three interacting causes of boundary rollback and Pointer Lock instability:\n\n1. **Chromium/OS Boundary Cursor-Warp Rollback Spikes (`movementX` / `movementY`)**:\n   - Even while `document.pointerLockElement === canvas` is active, Chromium\'s non-raw Pointer Lock implementation (in iframes, macOS, Linux/Wayland/X11, scaled viewports, and virtualized displays) warps the hidden cursor back toward the lock center when it reaches a screen or iframe edge, emitting an opposite-direction `mousemove` spike equal to `center - edge` (e.g., `-250px` to `-550px` in preview panes).\n   - `InputManager.handleMouseMove` previously only dropped deltas `> 600px`, allowing every viewport/iframe edge warp jump (`<= 600px`) straight into `FlightController`, instantly snapping/rolling the ship and camera backward.\n\n2. **`unadjustedMovement: true` Async Rejection & `pointerlockerror` Loop**:\n   - Live Chromium testing showed `canvas.requestPointerLock({ unadjustedMovement: true })` immediately rejected with `NotSupportedError` and fired a `pointerlockerror` event, forcing an asynchronous fallback call inside `.catch()` (outside the synchronous user-gesture stack) and transiently resetting `pointerLocked` state.\n\n3. **Duplicate `mousedown` / Pointer Lock Listeners & Missing Target Ownership Verification**:\n   - `FlightCanvas` (`div` `onMouseDown`) and `InputManager` (`window` `mousedown`) both invoked `requestPointerLock()` on the same click.\n   - `InputManager` lacked an attachment guard against duplicate listener registration, checked `Boolean(document.pointerLockElement)` rather than verifying `document.pointerLockElement === this.lockTarget`, and could invoke `onPauseRequested` twice when pressing `Escape`.\n\n*(Verified clean: `FlightController`, `CameraController`, and `CombatManager` use unbounded local-space quaternion turning and 3D world-space camera tracking with no cursor recentering or screen-edge clamping.)*\n\n---\n\n## 2. Relevant Code Locations\n- `src/engine/InputManager.ts`\n- `src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx`\n- `src/App.tsx`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exact Fix Applied\n- **`src/engine/InputManager.ts`**:\n  - **Synchronous Standard Pointer Lock**: Removed `{ unadjustedMovement: true }` so `requestPointerLock()` runs synchronously on `this.lockTarget` without `NotSupportedError` rejections or spurious `pointerlockerror` events.\n  - **Strict Ownership Verification (`isLockOwned`)**: Verifies `document.pointerLockElement === this.lockTarget` in `pointerlockchange`, `pointerlockerror`, `handleMouseMove`, `handleMouseDown`, and `consumeSnapshot()`.\n  - **Boundary Cursor-Warp Rollback Filtering (`isAnomalousWarpJump`)**: Filters anomalous single-event warp spikes (`|raw| > 350` or sudden opposite-sign jumps `>= 90px` exceeding `3.2x` recent sustained directional movement) while passing 100% of fine micro-movements (`1\342\200\2235px`), continuous sweeps, and smooth human direction reversals without clamping or recentering.\n  - **Single-Listener Lifecycle & Pause Deduplication**: Guarded `attach()` against duplicate listener registration, ensured `detach()` removes all listeners and exits owned Pointer Lock on unmount, and deduplicated `Escape` pause invocation across synchronous/asynchronous `pointerlockchange` timing.\n- **`src/scene/FlightCanvas.tsx` & `src/App.tsx`**:\n  - Removed the duplicate `onMouseDown` wrapper handler and `onCanvasClick` prop so `InputManager` is the sole owner of canvas mouse & Pointer Lock input.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Pointer-Lock & Build Verification\n- **Production Build (`vite build`) & Type Check (`tsc --noEmit`)**: Both passed with 0 errors.\n- **Unit & Simulation Verification (`npx tsx`)**:\n  - Verified duplicate `attach()` prevention and full listener removal + lock release on `detach()`.\n  - Verified non-canvas `pointerLockElement` rejection (`isPointerLocked() === false`).\n  - Verified continuous 120-frame rightward turning (`231.9\302\260` total rotation) with injected `-420px` and `-260px` edge warp spikes cleanly filtered (`warpSpikesFiltered: 2`), `0.254\302\260` fine micro-precision (`2px` input), intact human smooth reversals, and single-fire `Escape` pause.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Actual Browser Test Results (Headless Chromium via Playwright)\nExecuted live end-to-end tests in Chromium (`1280\303\227720` top-level and `1024\303\227640` `<iframe>` with `allow=\"pointer-lock\"`):\n1. **Pointer Lock Engagement**: Entered gameplay (`M-01`) -> `document.pointerLockElement === \"CANVAS\"`, **`0` `pointerlockerror` events**, and the engage prompt remained hidden.\n2. **Iframe Support**: Verified `document.pointerLockElement === \"CANVAS\"` inside a `1024\303\227640` embedded `<iframe>`.\n3. **Continuous Mouse Turning & Edge Warp Suppression**: Dispatched continuous relative `mousemove` sweeps (`movementX: +20`, `movementY: -12`, fine `+2px`) alongside a simulated `-420px` edge-warp spike -> HUD attitude advanced smoothly from `HDG 000\302\260 / PITCH +0\302\260` to `HDG 047\302\260` and `HDG 050\302\260 / PITCH +15\302\260` with zero rollback.\n4. **Keyboard Flight Controls**: `W + Shift + A` accelerated to `42 m/s` (`BOOSTING`) and rolled to `ROLL +15\302\260` as expected.\n5. **ESC Release & Resume**: `Escape` released Pointer Lock (`document.pointerLockElement === null`) and opened `Flight Paused`; clicking `Resume Flight` re-locked `\"CANVAS\"` with `0` errors.\n\n*Note*: Automated browser verification ran in headless Chromium (SwiftShader) using DOM/Playwright events; a final manual check with a physical desktop mouse in your target preview browser is recommended to confirm OS-level hardware feel."
