  planner_response {
    response: "# STARFALL \342\200\224 Mouse Boundary Rollback Root Cause & Fix Report\n\n## 1. Why the Previous Two Attempts Failed\n- **Attempt 1 (Phase 3)** misdiagnosed the rollback as an FPS-style mouselook issue and **deleted the persistent aim cursor state entirely**, replacing it with a transient delta buffer (`pendingYawRad` / `pendingPitchRad`) that decayed to `0` at `24/s` whenever physical mouse motion paused. Meanwhile, `CombatManager.projectHudTelemetry()` projected the ship\'s nose onto the lagging chase camera to position the reticle. As soon as your hand stopped at the edge, turning stopped and the reticle slid right back to screen center (`640px`).\n- **Attempt 2** only modified `InputManager.ts` (Pointer Lock request/listener cleanup and warp-spike filtering) without touching `FlightController.ts`, `CombatManager.ts`, or `FlightHUD.tsx`, leaving the transient turn decay and reticle rollback to screen center completely untouched.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The Actual Root Cause (Confirmed in Live Browser Trace)\nLive Chromium telemetry confirmed Pointer Lock **was** active on `CANVAS`, and the rollback occurred inside **game-side input/reticle processing**, not browser Pointer Lock failure:\n1. **`FlightController.ts` used decaying impulse turning (`pendingYawRad -= stepYaw`) instead of a persistent virtual steering cursor**: when physical mouse movement paused at an edge (`movementX === 0`), `pendingYawRad` decayed to `0` in ~150 ms and stopped ship rotation.\n2. **`CombatManager.ts` overwrote `telemetry.aimScreenX` / `telemetry.aimScreenY` every frame** with the 3D ship nose projected onto the lagging chase camera. When the ship stopped turning, `CameraController` caught up and pulled the only visible reticle on screen directly back to the center (`757px -> 698px -> 655px -> 640px` on a `1280px` viewport).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exact Files & Code Responsible\n- `src/engine/FlightController.ts` \342\200\224 `pendingYawRad` / `pendingPitchRad` exponential decay (`responseRate = 24.0`, `pendingYawRad -= stepYaw`) and velocity-derived `aimNormalizedX/Y`.\n- `src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts` \342\200\224 `projectHudTelemetry()` overwriting `telemetry.aimScreenX` and `telemetry.aimScreenY` with the ship-nose camera projection.\n- `src/components/FlightHUD.tsx` \342\200\224 rendered only the camera-projected nose reticle rather than a persistent virtual mouse steering cursor + separate 3D cannon boresight.\n- `src/engine/InputManager.ts` \342\200\224 overly strict `90px` opposite-sign filter that could discard fast human reversals.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What Changed\n- **`src/engine/FlightController.ts`**:\n  - Replaced decaying `pendingYawRad`/`pendingPitchRad` with a **persistent virtual mouse steering cursor** (`aimCursorX`, `aimCursorY`) in normalized viewport coordinates `[-0.96, +0.96] \303\227 [-0.94, +0.94]`, updated strictly by relative Pointer Lock deltas (`mouseDeltaX`, `mouseDeltaY`) scaled by `settings.mouseSensitivity` and `settings.invertY`.\n  - **Zero auto-recentering and zero rollback**: once moved to any screen edge, `(aimCursorX, aimCursorY)` stays pinned there until you move the mouse back toward center, continuously driving smooth `yawVelocity` / `pitchVelocity` (with a small `0.02` center deadzone and precision curve near center for fine gunnery).\n  - Writes `telemetry.aimScreenX` / `telemetry.aimScreenY` directly from `(aimCursorX, aimCursorY)`.\n  - Added subtle forward weapon gimbal convergence in `getAimDirectionWorld()` (`\302\2610.14 rad` yaw / `\302\2610.11 rad` pitch) and `centerAimCursor()` for clean unpausing.\n  - Left thrust, max speed, boost, `A/D` roll, and `CameraController.ts` untouched.\n- **`src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts`**:\n  - Stopped `projectHudTelemetry()` from overwriting `telemetry.aimScreenX` / `telemetry.aimScreenY`; retained `boresightScreenX` / `boresightScreenY` for the ship\'s 3D cannon convergence point and target lock ranking.\n- **`src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`**:\n  - Renders the **persistent virtual mouse steering cursor** at `(aimScreenX, aimScreenY)`, a subtle **steering vector tether** from center when deflected, and a separate **3D cannon boresight reticle** at `(boresightScreenX, boresightScreenY)` with hit/kill markers.\n- **`src/engine/InputManager.ts` & `src/App.tsx`**:\n  - Simplified `handleMouseMove` to pass all legitimate relative deltas (retaining only a `> 500px` single-event OS glitch guard) and called `flightRef.current.centerAimCursor()` inside `handleResume()`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Evidence from Browser Testing (Headless Chromium, `1280\303\227720`)\n\n### Before Fix (Reproduced Live Rollback)\n- Moving right (`+35px \303\227 15 frames`): `reticleX` reached `757`, `hdg: 68\302\260`.\n- Holding stationary at edge (`30 frames`): `reticleX` rolled back `757 -> 698 -> 655 -> 640` (exact center) and `hdg` froze at `71\302\260`.\n\n### After Fix (Verified Across All 4 Screen Edges)\n- **Pointer Lock**: `document.pointerLockElement === \"CANVAS\"` throughout active gameplay.\n- **Right Edge (`1254px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorX: 1254`, `hdg: 13\302\260`\n  - +12 frames stationary: `cursorX: 1254` (**0px rollback**), `hdg: 67\302\260`\n  - +27 frames stationary: `cursorX: 1254` (**0px rollback**), `hdg: 157\302\260` (continuous turning)\n- **Left Edge (`26px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorX: 26`, `hdg: 158\302\260` -> +20 frames stationary: `cursorX: 26` (**0px rollback**), `hdg: 42\302\260`\n- **Top Edge (`22px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorY: 22`, `pitch: +21\302\260` -> +18 frames stationary: `cursorY: 22` (**0px rollback**), continuously pitched over the top (`pitch: +63\302\260`, `roll: 178\302\260`)\n- **Bottom Edge (`698px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorY: 698`, `pitch: +63\302\260` -> +18 frames stationary: `cursorY: 698` (**0px rollback**), continuously pitched back down (`pitch: +21\302\260`, `roll: 2\302\260`)\n- **Return to Center (`635, 362`)**: Turning stopped cleanly (`hdg: 17\302\260`, `pitch: -1\302\260` steady across 15 idle frames).\n- **ESC / Resume & Build**: `Escape` released Pointer Lock (`null`) and paused; `Resume Flight` re-locked `CANVAS`; `vite build` and `tsc --noEmit` both passed with `0` errors.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Resolution Status\n**Genuinely fixed and verified in Chromium across all four screen edges.** The mouse cursor now stays pinned at any screen edge you move it to and continuously turns the spaceship and camera until you move the mouse back toward the center. (A quick check with your physical desktop mouse in the preview window is still recommended to confirm comfort and sensitivity preference.)"
    message_id: "8RT_apPCLu-2sOIPidCwkAQ"
    modified_response: "# STARFALL \342\200\224 Mouse Boundary Rollback Root Cause & Fix Report\n\n## 1. Why the Previous Two Attempts Failed\n- **Attempt 1 (Phase 3)** misdiagnosed the rollback as an FPS-style mouselook issue and **deleted the persistent aim cursor state entirely**, replacing it with a transient delta buffer (`pendingYawRad` / `pendingPitchRad`) that decayed to `0` at `24/s` whenever physical mouse motion paused. Meanwhile, `CombatManager.projectHudTelemetry()` projected the ship\'s nose onto the lagging chase camera to position the reticle. As soon as your hand stopped at the edge, turning stopped and the reticle slid right back to screen center (`640px`).\n- **Attempt 2** only modified `InputManager.ts` (Pointer Lock request/listener cleanup and warp-spike filtering) without touching `FlightController.ts`, `CombatManager.ts`, or `FlightHUD.tsx`, leaving the transient turn decay and reticle rollback to screen center completely untouched.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The Actual Root Cause (Confirmed in Live Browser Trace)\nLive Chromium telemetry confirmed Pointer Lock **was** active on `CANVAS`, and the rollback occurred inside **game-side input/reticle processing**, not browser Pointer Lock failure:\n1. **`FlightController.ts` used decaying impulse turning (`pendingYawRad -= stepYaw`) instead of a persistent virtual steering cursor**: when physical mouse movement paused at an edge (`movementX === 0`), `pendingYawRad` decayed to `0` in ~150 ms and stopped ship rotation.\n2. **`CombatManager.ts` overwrote `telemetry.aimScreenX` / `telemetry.aimScreenY` every frame** with the 3D ship nose projected onto the lagging chase camera. When the ship stopped turning, `CameraController` caught up and pulled the only visible reticle on screen directly back to the center (`757px -> 698px -> 655px -> 640px` on a `1280px` viewport).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exact Files & Code Responsible\n- `src/engine/FlightController.ts` \342\200\224 `pendingYawRad` / `pendingPitchRad` exponential decay (`responseRate = 24.0`, `pendingYawRad -= stepYaw`) and velocity-derived `aimNormalizedX/Y`.\n- `src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts` \342\200\224 `projectHudTelemetry()` overwriting `telemetry.aimScreenX` and `telemetry.aimScreenY` with the ship-nose camera projection.\n- `src/components/FlightHUD.tsx` \342\200\224 rendered only the camera-projected nose reticle rather than a persistent virtual mouse steering cursor + separate 3D cannon boresight.\n- `src/engine/InputManager.ts` \342\200\224 overly strict `90px` opposite-sign filter that could discard fast human reversals.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What Changed\n- **`src/engine/FlightController.ts`**:\n  - Replaced decaying `pendingYawRad`/`pendingPitchRad` with a **persistent virtual mouse steering cursor** (`aimCursorX`, `aimCursorY`) in normalized viewport coordinates `[-0.96, +0.96] \303\227 [-0.94, +0.94]`, updated strictly by relative Pointer Lock deltas (`mouseDeltaX`, `mouseDeltaY`) scaled by `settings.mouseSensitivity` and `settings.invertY`.\n  - **Zero auto-recentering and zero rollback**: once moved to any screen edge, `(aimCursorX, aimCursorY)` stays pinned there until you move the mouse back toward center, continuously driving smooth `yawVelocity` / `pitchVelocity` (with a small `0.02` center deadzone and precision curve near center for fine gunnery).\n  - Writes `telemetry.aimScreenX` / `telemetry.aimScreenY` directly from `(aimCursorX, aimCursorY)`.\n  - Added subtle forward weapon gimbal convergence in `getAimDirectionWorld()` (`\302\2610.14 rad` yaw / `\302\2610.11 rad` pitch) and `centerAimCursor()` for clean unpausing.\n  - Left thrust, max speed, boost, `A/D` roll, and `CameraController.ts` untouched.\n- **`src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts`**:\n  - Stopped `projectHudTelemetry()` from overwriting `telemetry.aimScreenX` / `telemetry.aimScreenY`; retained `boresightScreenX` / `boresightScreenY` for the ship\'s 3D cannon convergence point and target lock ranking.\n- **`src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`**:\n  - Renders the **persistent virtual mouse steering cursor** at `(aimScreenX, aimScreenY)`, a subtle **steering vector tether** from center when deflected, and a separate **3D cannon boresight reticle** at `(boresightScreenX, boresightScreenY)` with hit/kill markers.\n- **`src/engine/InputManager.ts` & `src/App.tsx`**:\n  - Simplified `handleMouseMove` to pass all legitimate relative deltas (retaining only a `> 500px` single-event OS glitch guard) and called `flightRef.current.centerAimCursor()` inside `handleResume()`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Evidence from Browser Testing (Headless Chromium, `1280\303\227720`)\n\n### Before Fix (Reproduced Live Rollback)\n- Moving right (`+35px \303\227 15 frames`): `reticleX` reached `757`, `hdg: 68\302\260`.\n- Holding stationary at edge (`30 frames`): `reticleX` rolled back `757 -> 698 -> 655 -> 640` (exact center) and `hdg` froze at `71\302\260`.\n\n### After Fix (Verified Across All 4 Screen Edges)\n- **Pointer Lock**: `document.pointerLockElement === \"CANVAS\"` throughout active gameplay.\n- **Right Edge (`1254px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorX: 1254`, `hdg: 13\302\260`\n  - +12 frames stationary: `cursorX: 1254` (**0px rollback**), `hdg: 67\302\260`\n  - +27 frames stationary: `cursorX: 1254` (**0px rollback**), `hdg: 157\302\260` (continuous turning)\n- **Left Edge (`26px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorX: 26`, `hdg: 158\302\260` -> +20 frames stationary: `cursorX: 26` (**0px rollback**), `hdg: 42\302\260`\n- **Top Edge (`22px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorY: 22`, `pitch: +21\302\260` -> +18 frames stationary: `cursorY: 22` (**0px rollback**), continuously pitched over the top (`pitch: +63\302\260`, `roll: 178\302\260`)\n- **Bottom Edge (`698px`) \342\200\224 held stationary**:\n  - Arrival: `cursorY: 698`, `pitch: +63\302\260` -> +18 frames stationary: `cursorY: 698` (**0px rollback**), continuously pitched back down (`pitch: +21\302\260`, `roll: 2\302\260`)\n- **Return to Center (`635, 362`)**: Turning stopped cleanly (`hdg: 17\302\260`, `pitch: -1\302\260` steady across 15 idle frames).\n- **ESC / Resume & Build**: `Escape` released Pointer Lock (`null`) and paused; `Resume Flight` re-locked `CANVAS`; `vite build` and `tsc --noEmit` both passed with `0` errors.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Resolution Status\n**Genuinely fixed and verified in Chromium across all four screen edges.** The mouse cursor now stays pinned at any screen edge you move it to and continuously turns the spaceship and camera until you move the mouse back toward the center. (A quick check with your physical desktop mouse in the preview window is still recommended to confirm comfort and sensitivity preference.)"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\324\002\n\321\002\001i\024}\023t+\035\214\254\004\270\272\003O\376\276\356O\305\315\254\230W \376uB\226\343J\023\342\035\336\307\234\021\272\275\017\343\002\307\221\260\304\213\211\205\356\2513\251W\205\265\367\365\222\241\264<C_\253\343\252\\\v\357v\'+(\036\av\205/\224\212\245n\260\314\005\004\252\366\tw\210\326\325S\nI\313\236^l\352\363oNi\220\335\273\227Q\241h=\000b\023\366hAk\b\346?\317\r>\246\031\231\303c8\244\n\361\250\nx\203\334\365\022\fV0\n?\257\371AG\350y\252O\354\031v\312\275c\2657\255_\222F\205_\0332So\243\322C+qm\213\356[4E\026\031Wl2\003\321\256KP\364\3149\020\317\236\001L\265\'\364\354A\"\220U\340\036\035tT\222t\364\an\246\321\340\361\0275\000oT_o\235\254\373\306\346F[oP\256\354\361@\022LS\267B\263d\372\276\215\232{\255\256S\021\f\000\260\315\273I\213}\036\262\024\2101\265\363\227\a\255\020!\"\335\254SKM\243ab*\022\033lI_/\215w\b\f\373\f\333\222\017\300\244PCps\r\\\311\237\325V@\034-\234\340x\316\372`\273\346\237\240\306T\316\242W"
