  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n# STARFALL \342\200\224 Flight Feel Restoration & Mouse Aim Boundary Tuning Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Task Overview\nThe user confirmed the **mouse boundary rollback issue is now fixed**, and requested a targeted follow-up task: **STARFALL \342\200\224 Flight Feel Restoration & Mouse Aim Boundary Tuning**.\n\n### Core Objectives & Requirements\n1. **Preserve the Successful Mouse Input Fix**:\n   - Keep working Pointer Lock (`document.pointerLockElement === canvas`) + relative `movementX`/`movementY` input (`InputManager.ts`).\n   - Do NOT reintroduce cursor recentering, auto-rollback, or absolute screen coordinate dependencies.\n   - Maintain continuous mouse steering at all physical screen edges.\n2. **Restore Original Flight Handling Feel**:\n   - Restore snappy, predictable Phase 1/2 arcade flight responsiveness, controlled inertia, frame-rate-independent delta-time handling, smooth chase camera follow, and intact boost behavior.\n3. **Implement a Bounded Virtual Aim Region**:\n   - Configurable horizontal and vertical aiming limits (`VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG`).\n   - Keep the virtual reticle inside a reasonable central region of the screen (not extreme screen edges/HUD).\n   - Smooth, predictable boundary clamping without sudden snapping or dead-travel overflow when leaving the boundary.\n   - Ship continues turning smoothly when the reticle is held on the boundary.\n4. **Camera & Flight Integration**:\n   - Single mouse input owner (`InputManager` -> `FlightController` -> `CameraController` follows ship).\n   - Clear separation between aim offset and ship rotation.\n5. **Actual Browser Verification (REQUIRED before reporting success)**:\n   - Verify all 7 acceptance items in headless Chromium (`playwright` at `/usr/local/share/bun-global/node_modules`) against `http://localhost:3000/`:\n     1. Continuous mouse movement at all physical screen edges (Pointer Lock active on `CANVAS`).\n     2. Virtual reticle stays strictly inside the configured bounded aiming region (`[25%..75%]` X, `[24%..76%]` Y; `[320..960] \303\227 [173..547]` on `1280\303\227720`).\n     3. Ship continues turning continuously when the reticle reaches and stays at the boundary (all 4 edges + diagonals), and pulls inward immediately on reversal with zero dead-travel.\n     4. Normal steering feels snappy, responsive, and frame-rate consistent (test 30Hz vs 60Hz vs 120Hz delta-time consistency).\n     5. Camera follow remains stable.\n     6. Boost behavior remains intact (`W + Shift` speed, boost energy drain, status `\'BOOSTING\'`).\n     7. Zero regression to the mouse boundary rollback issue.\n6. **Final Report (6 required items)**:\n   1. Why flight handling became worse.\n   2. Which changes caused the regression.\n   3. How the virtual aiming boundary works.\n   4. Which original flight characteristics were restored.\n   5. Actual browser testing results.\n   6. Any remaining issues.\n\n### Scope Constraints\n- Do NOT redesign the game or touch unrelated combat, bot AI, mission, or UI systems.\n- Do NOT replace the working Pointer Lock implementation in `InputManager.ts`.\n- Do NOT add dependencies.\n\n## 2. Progress\n\n### Completed Code Edits (NOT YET COMPILED, LINTED, OR TESTED)\n1. **`/src/engine/FlightController.ts`** (edited & saved):\n   - Exported `VirtualAimConfig` and `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG`:\n     - `maxScreenOffsetX: 0.25` (keeps reticle within `[25%..75%]` viewport width, i.e., `320px\342\200\223960px` on `1280px`)\n     - `maxScreenOffsetY: 0.26` (keeps reticle within `[24%..76%]` viewport height, i.e., `173px\342\200\223547px` on `720px`)\n     - `pixelsToBoundary: 210` (halved from the sluggish `420px` so normal wrist moves reach full authority crisply)\n     - `deadzone: 0.03` (drift-free straight flight at center)\n     - `responseExponent: 1.25` (replaces sluggish `0.35*e + 0.65*e^2` curve for immediate small/medium turn authority)\n   - Replaced rectangular box clamp (`\302\2610.96 \303\227 \302\2610.94`) with smooth **radial unit-circle clamp** (`hypot(nextX, nextY) <= 1.0`): prevents corner dead-travel, allows smooth gliding around the perimeter, eliminates hidden overflow beyond `r = 1.0` so reversing inward responds on pixel 1, and NEVER auto-recenters or rolls back.\n   - Restored snappy arcade angular response & controlled inertia: `responseLambda = profile.angularDamping * (isSteering ? 2.1 : 1.8)` (up from `1.45`) with frame-rate-independent `1 - Math.exp(-responseLambda * safeDt)`, preserving original `SHIP_CONFIGS.interceptor.flight` speeds (`yawSpeed: 2.1`, `pitchSpeed: 1.95`, `rollSpeed: 3.1`, `angularDamping: 7.5`, boost & linear thrust untouched).\n   - Updated forward weapon gimbal limits to `GIMBAL_MAX_YAW_RAD = 0.24`, `GIMBAL_MAX_PITCH_RAD = 0.17` to align well with the bounded combat envelope.\n   - Mapped `telemetry.aimScreenX = 0.5 + this.aimCursorX * VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG.maxScreenOffsetX` and `telemetry.aimScreenY = 0.5 + this.aimCursorY * VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG.maxScreenOffsetY`.\n2. **`/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`** (edited & saved):\n   - Imported `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG`.\n   - Added `aimBoundaryRef` rendering a subtle, unobtrusive elliptical boundary ring (`width: 50vw`, `height: 52vh`, opacity `0.06` at rest rising smoothly up to `0.26` near boundary) synced 1:1 with `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG`.\n   - Adjusted steering tether opacity normalization divisor from `260` to `220` to match the tighter bounded region.\n\n### Files Inspected & Confirmed Clean (No Edits Needed)\n- `/src/config/ships.ts` \342\200\224 Original Phase 1 `SHIP_CONFIGS.interceptor.flight` values intact (`maxSpeed: 135`, `acceleration: 95`, `boostMultiplier: 1.85`, `boostAccelMultiplier: 2.35`, `yawSpeed: 2.1`, `pitchSpeed: 1.95`, `rollSpeed: 3.1`, `angularDamping: 7.5`).\n- `/src/engine/InputManager.ts` \342\200\224 Clean synchronous Pointer Lock on `this.lockTarget` (`CANVAS`), `isLockOwned()` verification, pure relative `movementX`/`movementY` (only `>500px` glitch guard), deduplicated listeners, clean `detach()`.\n- `/src/engine/CameraController.ts` \342\200\224 Single-responsibility chase camera following `flight` state only (does NOT read mouse input directly; preserves `rotAlpha = 1 - exp(-13 * camSens * dt)`, `posLambda`, boost FOV `62 -> 78.5`).\n- `/src/engine/combat/CombatManager.ts` \342\200\224 Preserves `telemetry.aimScreenX/Y` owned by `FlightController`; projects 3D cannon convergence onto `boresightScreenX/Y`.\n- `/skills/system_skills/threejs/SKILL.md` \342\200\224 Already read earlier in session.\n\n### Not Yet Done\n- Build & TypeScript check (`compile_applet` + `lint_applet`).\n- Restart dev server (`restart_dev_server`).\n- Automated frame-rate independence & response curve unit check (`npx tsx`).\n- Live headless Chromium browser verification via Playwright covering all 7 acceptance criteria.\n- Deliver the final 6-point report to the user.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Root Cause of Flight Handling Regression**:\n  1. `CURSOR_PIXELS_TO_EDGE = 420` + heavy quadratic curve `e * (0.35 + 0.65 * e)` made normal mouse movements feel severely sluggish (e.g., a `50px` movement only gave ~5% turn rate, and a `105px` movement only ~12.8% turn rate; reversing from edge required dragging `420px` back).\n  2. `CURSOR_EDGE_X = 0.96` / `CURSOR_EDGE_Y = 0.94` allowed the reticle to travel all the way to the extreme monitor edges (`26px..1254px`, `22px..698px`), overlapping top/bottom HUD elements and creating rectangular corner distortion.\n  3. Lower `turnAlpha` damping multiplier (`angularDamping * 1.45`) compounded the sluggish feeling on top of the long cursor travel.\n- **No Git Repo**: Workspace has no `.git` directory (`fatal: not a git repository`), so original Phase 1 parameters were verified from `SHIP_CONFIGS` in `/src/config/ships.ts` and existing `CameraController.ts` / `FlightController.ts` sections.\n- **Playwright in Sandbox**: Playwright is available via `NODE_PATH=/usr/local/share/bun-global/node_modules node -e \'...\'` using headless Chromium with `args: [\"--no-sandbox\", \"--use-gl=angle\", \"--use-angle=swiftshader\"]`. Setting Low graphics preset in `localStorage` (`starfall.settings.v2`) makes SwiftShader load & render fast in ~5\342\200\2238 seconds.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- Earlier in session: `FlightController.ts` initially had FPS-style decaying `pendingYawRad`/`pendingPitchRad` and `CombatManager` overwrote `aimScreenX/Y` with camera-lagging ship nose projection, causing the reticle to roll back to center (`640px`) and stopping turns when held at edge. Fixed in previous turn by switching to persistent virtual steering cursor driven by relative Pointer Lock deltas.\n- Earlier in session: `InputManager.ts` had `requestPointerLock({ unadjustedMovement: true })` causing `NotSupportedError` and `pointerlockerror` in Chromium, plus duplicate `onMouseDown` in `FlightCanvas.tsx` and double-fire `Escape` pause. All fixed and verified with 0 `pointerlockerror` events.\n- No unresolved errors currently exist; the new edits in `FlightController.ts` and `FlightHUD.tsx` simply have not been compiled/tested yet.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running on port 3000, but needs `restart_dev_server` (or Vite will serve updated files, still best to compile + restart before browser test).\n- Modified files ready for verification: `/src/engine/FlightController.ts` and `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`.\n- No temporary files exist on disk.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (Execute Immediately in Priority Order)\n1. **Compile & Lint**: Run `compile_applet` (and `lint_applet` to check TypeScript errors early), then `restart_dev_server` so port 3000 serves the updated code cleanly.\n2. **Unit Verification (`npx tsx`)**: Run a quick inline `npx tsx -e` verification script checking:\n   - Frame-rate independence: identical yaw rotation after 1.0s at 30 Hz, 60 Hz, and 120 Hz (`< 1\302\260` variance).\n   - Smooth elliptical boundary clamping: pushing `+1000px` right keeps `hypot(aimCursorX, aimCursorY) === 1.0` (`aimScreenX === 0.75`), pulling `-10px` left immediately moves `aimCursorX < 1.0` on the very first frame (zero dead-travel overflow), and diagonal pushes stay on `r === 1.0`.\n   - Responsiveness comparison: `105px` move produces ~40% turn rate (snappy vs old ~12.8%).\n3. **Live Browser Verification (Headless Chromium via Playwright)**:\n   - Launch `http://localhost:3000/` (`1280\303\227720`, Low preset in `localStorage` for fast SwiftShader).\n   - Click `Campaign Missions` -> `Launch M-01` -> wait for `Hull Integrity`.\n   - Verify all 7 acceptance criteria in browser:\n     1. `document.pointerLockElement === \"CANVAS\"` with 0 `pointerlockerror` events and 0 page errors.\n     2. Right edge (`+600px` push): `[data-testid=\"virtual-mouse-cursor\"]` stops cleanly at `cursorX \342\211\210 960px` (`75%` of `1280px`, NOT `1254px`!), stays pinned with **0px rollback** while held stationary, and `HDG` continues turning continuously.\n     3. Left edge (`-1200px` push): cursor stays cleanly at `cursorX \342\211\210 320px` (`25%`), 0px rollback, `HDG` turns left continuously.\n     4. Top edge (`-600px` push): cursor stays cleanly at `cursorY \342\211\210 173px` (`24%` of `720px`), 0px rollback, `PITCH` pitches up continuously.\n     5. Bottom edge (`+1200px` push): cursor stays cleanly at `cursorY \342\211\210 547px` (`76%` of `720px`), 0px rollback, `PITCH` pitches down continuously.\n     6. Diagonal push (`+400px, -400px`): cursor stays strictly on the smooth ellipse perimeter (`((cx-640)/320)^2 + ((cy-360)/187.2)^2 <= 1.02`), NOT outside in screen corners.\n     7. Immediate reversal from boundary: small `-25px` inward move immediately moves cursor inward from `960px` on the next frame (zero dead-travel).\n     8. Boost check (`KeyW + ShiftLeft`): speed accelerates well past cruise (`> 45 m/s` within short hold), `Flight Status` reports `BOOSTING`, boost energy decreases.\n     9. `Escape` releases Pointer Lock & pauses; `Resume Flight` re-locks `CANVAS` centered at `(640, 360)`.\n4. **Final Verification Pair**: If any tweaks were made during testing, co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together before finishing.\n5. **Deliver Final Report**: Provide the concise, evidence-backed 6-section report requested by the user (1. Why flight handling became worse, 2. Which changes caused the regression, 3. How the virtual aiming boundary works, 4. Which original flight characteristics were restored, 5. Actual browser testing results with exact observed pixel/attitude values, 6. Any remaining issues).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Never claim functionality was tested unless actually executed and observed.\n- Do not modify unrelated combat, bot AI, mission, or UI systems.\n- Do not break the working Pointer Lock relative `movementX`/`movementY` input fix.\n- Keep final report concise, technically precise, and grounded in exact measured results (no hype, no internal IDs).\n</summary>"
