  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Yaw Rate Discrepancy**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The output shows `tel.yawRate` at 1.000, but the raw `yawSpeed` is 2.1. It turns out `tel.yawRate` is normalized (-1 to +1) based on `yawVelocity / profile.yawSpeed`, which is not what I expected. This explains the odd discrepancy I was seeing. I need to account for this normalization in my calculations going forward.\n\n\n**Calculating Yaw Rate Scaling**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `yawRate` scaling. It\'s now clear that pixel movements directly correlate to a percentage of the maximum yaw speed. At 50px, I get 14.6%, at 105px it\'s 40.4%, and at 210px I achieve the full 100%. Frame-rate independence is good, with only 0.35\302\260 of variance across different frame rates. Also, I\'m noting the clamp behavior at the edges of the screen and the effects of immediate reverse actions.\n\n\n**Considering Task Completion Timing**\n\nI\'m wrestling with the timing of stopping tool calls in relation to background tasks. It\'s tricky because I don\'t want to prematurely end my turn. The documentation clearly states to proceed with other work *or* stop calling tools after a command, but does \"stopping\" imply waiting for background processes? The timer is key to triggering the turn end. I\'m going to quickly check `FlightHUD.tsx` (lines 315-395) while Playwright completes its background task. The background task `task-385` is still running.\n\n\n"
