  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. Why Flight Handling Became Worse\n\nThe previous mouse-boundary rollback fix solved the Pointer Lock rollback bug, but introduced three steering-feel regressions:\n\n1. **Severely sluggish mouse steering authority**: Reaching full turn rate required dragging the mouse `420px` from center, and a heavy quadratic response curve (`e * (0.35 + 0.65 * e)`) suppressed small and medium movements (a `50px` wrist movement delivered only ~5% turn rate, and a `105px` movement only ~12.8%).\n2. **Unbounded screen-edge reticle travel**: The virtual cursor was allowed to travel all the way to `\302\26196%` horizontally (`26px..1254px` on `1280px`) and `\302\26194%` vertically (`22px..698px` on `720px`), overlapping HUD instruments and requiring large physical sweeps to reverse direction.\n3. **Over-damped angular acceleration**: The angular smoothing multiplier (`angularDamping * 1.45`) compounded the long cursor throw, making yaw and pitch initiation feel floaty compared to the original Phase 1/2 arcade response.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Changes That Caused the Regression\n\nAll three regressions originated inside `FlightController`:\n\n- `CURSOR_PIXELS_TO_EDGE = 420` (excessive throw distance from center to full turn rate).\n- `CURSOR_EDGE_X = 0.96` and `CURSOR_EDGE_Y = 0.94` with rectangular axis-by-axis clamping (`[-0.96..0.96] \303\227 [-0.94..0.94]`).\n- Heavy quadratic steering curve `effective * (0.35 + 0.65 * effective)` combined with the lower `angularDamping * 1.45` turn-rate smoothing factor.\n\nThe Pointer Lock pipeline in `InputManager`, the single-responsibility chase camera in `CameraController`, and ship stats in `SHIP_CONFIGS` were clean and preserved untouched.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How the Virtual Aiming Boundary Works\n\nA configurable `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG` now defines a compact central combat envelope independent of physical monitor edges:\n\n- **Screen envelope**: `maxScreenOffsetX: 0.25` (`[25%..75%]` viewport width, `320px..960px` at `1280\303\227720`) and `maxScreenOffsetY: 0.26` (`[24%..76%]` viewport height, `172.8px..547.2px` at `1280\303\227720`).\n- **Throw & response**: `pixelsToBoundary: 210` (halved from `420px`), `deadzone: 0.03`, and `responseExponent: 1.25`.\n- **Smooth radial unit-circle clamp**: Relative Pointer Lock deltas (`movementX`, `movementY`) update `(aimCursorX, aimCursorY)` and project any vector with `hypot(x, y) > 1.0` smoothly onto the unit circle (`r = 1.0`), mapped directly to the screen ellipse:\n  - `aimScreenX = 0.5 + aimCursorX * 0.25`\n  - `aimScreenY = 0.5 + aimCursorY * 0.26`\n- **Zero rollback & zero dead-travel**: The cursor never auto-recenters while flying; holding it on the boundary sustains continuous 360\302\260+ yaw/pitch rotation, and because no hidden overflow accumulates beyond `r = 1.0`, pulling inward responds on the very first pixel of reversed mouse movement.\n- **Visual cue**: `FlightHUD` renders a subtle elliptical boundary ring synced 1:1 with `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG` (`opacity: 0.06` at rest, rising smoothly up to `0.26` near the limit) and initializes reticle transforms at viewport center to eliminate any first-frame top-left flash on mount or resume.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Original Flight Characteristics Restored\n\n- **Snappy arcade steering authority**: `50px` mouse movement now delivers `14.6%` max turn rate (`0.307 rad/s`), `105px` delivers `40.4%` (`0.848 rad/s`), and `210px` reaches `100%` (`2.100 rad/s`), while keeping fine precision near center via the `3%` deadzone and `1.25` exponent.\n- **Crisp angular responsiveness with controlled inertia**: Restored angular response factor to `angularDamping * 2.1` while steering and `angularDamping * 1.8` while leveling, using frame-rate-independent `1 - Math.exp(-lambda * dt)`.\n- **Original ship flight & boost profiles intact**: Preserved `SHIP_CONFIGS.interceptor.flight` (`maxSpeed: 135`, `acceleration: 95`, `boostMultiplier: 1.85`, `boostAccelMultiplier: 2.35`, `yawSpeed: 2.1`, `pitchSpeed: 1.95`, `rollSpeed: 3.1`, `angularDamping: 7.5`) and chase camera follow/boost FOV (`62\302\260 \342\206\222 78.5\302\260`).\n- **Aligned forward gimbal**: Tuned cannon gimbal limits (`GIMBAL_MAX_YAW_RAD = 0.24`, `GIMBAL_MAX_PITCH_RAD = 0.17`) to match the bounded combat envelope cleanly.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Actual Verification Results\n\n#### Build & Static Checks\n- **Production build**: Passed (`compile_applet` succeeded).\n- **TypeScript check**: Passed (`tsc --noEmit`, 0 errors).\n\n#### Simulation Physics Verification (`tsx`)\n- **Frame-rate consistency** (`105px` right held for `1.0s`):\n  - `30 Hz`: yaw `-46.29\302\260`\n  - `60 Hz`: yaw `-45.94\302\260`\n  - `120 Hz`: yaw `-45.75\302\260`\n  - Max variance across 30\342\200\223120 Hz: **`0.35\302\260`**.\n- **Boundary clamp & reversal**: `+1000px` right clamped to `aimCursorX = 1.0` (`aimScreenX = 0.7500`); immediate `-10px` reversal moved `aimCursorX` to `0.9524` (`aimScreenX = 0.7381`) on frame 1.\n- **Diagonal clamp**: `+500px, -500px` clamped to exact radius `1.000000` (`ellipseEq = 1.000000`).\n- **Boost (`W + Shift`, `1.0s`)**: Reached `249.8 m/s`, `boostEnergy: 74`, `status: \'BOOSTING\'`.\n\n#### Live Headless Chromium Browser Verification (`1280\303\227720`, Mission M-01)\n- **Pointer Lock**: Acquired on `CANVAS`, `0` `pointerlockerror` events, `0` page errors, `0` console errors.\n- **Initial state**: Reticle centered at `(640.0, 360.0)`, `HDG 0\302\260`, `PITCH 0\302\260`.\n- **Right boundary (`+400px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `X = 960.0` (`75.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `HDG` turned continuously from `8\302\260 \342\206\222 37\302\260`.\n- **Immediate reversal (`-25px` left)**: Cursor immediately pulled inward from `960.0 \342\206\222 921.9` on the next frame (matches `960 - (25/210)*320 = 921.9px`, zero dead-travel).\n- **Left boundary (`-600px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `X = 320.0` (`25.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `HDG` turned continuously left `44\302\260 \342\206\222 15\302\260`.\n- **Top boundary (`-600px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `Y = 172.8` (`24.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `PITCH` pitched continuously upward `+7\302\260 \342\206\222 +29\302\260`.\n- **Bottom boundary (`+600px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `Y = 547.2` (`76.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `PITCH` pitched continuously downward `+19\302\260 \342\206\222 -3\302\260`.\n- **Diagonal push (`+300px, -300px`)**: Clamped smoothly on the elliptical perimeter at `(866.3, 227.6)` (`((x-640)/320)\302\262 + ((y-360)/187.2)\302\262 = 1.0003`).\n- **Boost (`W + ShiftLeft`)**: Accelerated from `2 m/s` (`isBoosting: false`) to `76 m/s` (`isBoosting: true`) within 5 software-rendered frames.\n- **Pause & Resume**: `Escape` cleanly released Pointer Lock (`pointerLockElement: null`) and displayed the pause menu; clicking `Resume Flight` re-acquired Pointer Lock on `CANVAS` with the reticle centered at `(640.0, 360.0)`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Remaining Issues\n\n- None observed in build, unit checks, or headless Chromium testing. Subjective fine-tuning of `pixelsToBoundary` (`210`) or `maxScreenOffsetX/Y` (`0.25` / `0.26`) can be adjusted in one place via `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG` if you want an even tighter or wider envelope after live playtesting on your hardware mouse/DPI."
    message_id: "Zxv_auWKGvKp28oP2fqj8Qg"
    modified_response: "### 1. Why Flight Handling Became Worse\n\nThe previous mouse-boundary rollback fix solved the Pointer Lock rollback bug, but introduced three steering-feel regressions:\n\n1. **Severely sluggish mouse steering authority**: Reaching full turn rate required dragging the mouse `420px` from center, and a heavy quadratic response curve (`e * (0.35 + 0.65 * e)`) suppressed small and medium movements (a `50px` wrist movement delivered only ~5% turn rate, and a `105px` movement only ~12.8%).\n2. **Unbounded screen-edge reticle travel**: The virtual cursor was allowed to travel all the way to `\302\26196%` horizontally (`26px..1254px` on `1280px`) and `\302\26194%` vertically (`22px..698px` on `720px`), overlapping HUD instruments and requiring large physical sweeps to reverse direction.\n3. **Over-damped angular acceleration**: The angular smoothing multiplier (`angularDamping * 1.45`) compounded the long cursor throw, making yaw and pitch initiation feel floaty compared to the original Phase 1/2 arcade response.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Changes That Caused the Regression\n\nAll three regressions originated inside `FlightController`:\n\n- `CURSOR_PIXELS_TO_EDGE = 420` (excessive throw distance from center to full turn rate).\n- `CURSOR_EDGE_X = 0.96` and `CURSOR_EDGE_Y = 0.94` with rectangular axis-by-axis clamping (`[-0.96..0.96] \303\227 [-0.94..0.94]`).\n- Heavy quadratic steering curve `effective * (0.35 + 0.65 * effective)` combined with the lower `angularDamping * 1.45` turn-rate smoothing factor.\n\nThe Pointer Lock pipeline in `InputManager`, the single-responsibility chase camera in `CameraController`, and ship stats in `SHIP_CONFIGS` were clean and preserved untouched.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How the Virtual Aiming Boundary Works\n\nA configurable `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG` now defines a compact central combat envelope independent of physical monitor edges:\n\n- **Screen envelope**: `maxScreenOffsetX: 0.25` (`[25%..75%]` viewport width, `320px..960px` at `1280\303\227720`) and `maxScreenOffsetY: 0.26` (`[24%..76%]` viewport height, `172.8px..547.2px` at `1280\303\227720`).\n- **Throw & response**: `pixelsToBoundary: 210` (halved from `420px`), `deadzone: 0.03`, and `responseExponent: 1.25`.\n- **Smooth radial unit-circle clamp**: Relative Pointer Lock deltas (`movementX`, `movementY`) update `(aimCursorX, aimCursorY)` and project any vector with `hypot(x, y) > 1.0` smoothly onto the unit circle (`r = 1.0`), mapped directly to the screen ellipse:\n  - `aimScreenX = 0.5 + aimCursorX * 0.25`\n  - `aimScreenY = 0.5 + aimCursorY * 0.26`\n- **Zero rollback & zero dead-travel**: The cursor never auto-recenters while flying; holding it on the boundary sustains continuous 360\302\260+ yaw/pitch rotation, and because no hidden overflow accumulates beyond `r = 1.0`, pulling inward responds on the very first pixel of reversed mouse movement.\n- **Visual cue**: `FlightHUD` renders a subtle elliptical boundary ring synced 1:1 with `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG` (`opacity: 0.06` at rest, rising smoothly up to `0.26` near the limit) and initializes reticle transforms at viewport center to eliminate any first-frame top-left flash on mount or resume.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Original Flight Characteristics Restored\n\n- **Snappy arcade steering authority**: `50px` mouse movement now delivers `14.6%` max turn rate (`0.307 rad/s`), `105px` delivers `40.4%` (`0.848 rad/s`), and `210px` reaches `100%` (`2.100 rad/s`), while keeping fine precision near center via the `3%` deadzone and `1.25` exponent.\n- **Crisp angular responsiveness with controlled inertia**: Restored angular response factor to `angularDamping * 2.1` while steering and `angularDamping * 1.8` while leveling, using frame-rate-independent `1 - Math.exp(-lambda * dt)`.\n- **Original ship flight & boost profiles intact**: Preserved `SHIP_CONFIGS.interceptor.flight` (`maxSpeed: 135`, `acceleration: 95`, `boostMultiplier: 1.85`, `boostAccelMultiplier: 2.35`, `yawSpeed: 2.1`, `pitchSpeed: 1.95`, `rollSpeed: 3.1`, `angularDamping: 7.5`) and chase camera follow/boost FOV (`62\302\260 \342\206\222 78.5\302\260`).\n- **Aligned forward gimbal**: Tuned cannon gimbal limits (`GIMBAL_MAX_YAW_RAD = 0.24`, `GIMBAL_MAX_PITCH_RAD = 0.17`) to match the bounded combat envelope cleanly.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Actual Verification Results\n\n#### Build & Static Checks\n- **Production build**: Passed (`compile_applet` succeeded).\n- **TypeScript check**: Passed (`tsc --noEmit`, 0 errors).\n\n#### Simulation Physics Verification (`tsx`)\n- **Frame-rate consistency** (`105px` right held for `1.0s`):\n  - `30 Hz`: yaw `-46.29\302\260`\n  - `60 Hz`: yaw `-45.94\302\260`\n  - `120 Hz`: yaw `-45.75\302\260`\n  - Max variance across 30\342\200\223120 Hz: **`0.35\302\260`**.\n- **Boundary clamp & reversal**: `+1000px` right clamped to `aimCursorX = 1.0` (`aimScreenX = 0.7500`); immediate `-10px` reversal moved `aimCursorX` to `0.9524` (`aimScreenX = 0.7381`) on frame 1.\n- **Diagonal clamp**: `+500px, -500px` clamped to exact radius `1.000000` (`ellipseEq = 1.000000`).\n- **Boost (`W + Shift`, `1.0s`)**: Reached `249.8 m/s`, `boostEnergy: 74`, `status: \'BOOSTING\'`.\n\n#### Live Headless Chromium Browser Verification (`1280\303\227720`, Mission M-01)\n- **Pointer Lock**: Acquired on `CANVAS`, `0` `pointerlockerror` events, `0` page errors, `0` console errors.\n- **Initial state**: Reticle centered at `(640.0, 360.0)`, `HDG 0\302\260`, `PITCH 0\302\260`.\n- **Right boundary (`+400px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `X = 960.0` (`75.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `HDG` turned continuously from `8\302\260 \342\206\222 37\302\260`.\n- **Immediate reversal (`-25px` left)**: Cursor immediately pulled inward from `960.0 \342\206\222 921.9` on the next frame (matches `960 - (25/210)*320 = 921.9px`, zero dead-travel).\n- **Left boundary (`-600px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `X = 320.0` (`25.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `HDG` turned continuously left `44\302\260 \342\206\222 15\302\260`.\n- **Top boundary (`-600px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `Y = 172.8` (`24.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `PITCH` pitched continuously upward `+7\302\260 \342\206\222 +29\302\260`.\n- **Bottom boundary (`+600px` push, held 4 frames)**: Clamped at `Y = 547.2` (`76.0%`), **`0.0px` rollback**, `PITCH` pitched continuously downward `+19\302\260 \342\206\222 -3\302\260`.\n- **Diagonal push (`+300px, -300px`)**: Clamped smoothly on the elliptical perimeter at `(866.3, 227.6)` (`((x-640)/320)\302\262 + ((y-360)/187.2)\302\262 = 1.0003`).\n- **Boost (`W + ShiftLeft`)**: Accelerated from `2 m/s` (`isBoosting: false`) to `76 m/s` (`isBoosting: true`) within 5 software-rendered frames.\n- **Pause & Resume**: `Escape` cleanly released Pointer Lock (`pointerLockElement: null`) and displayed the pause menu; clicking `Resume Flight` re-acquired Pointer Lock on `CANVAS` with the reticle centered at `(640.0, 360.0)`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Remaining Issues\n\n- None observed in build, unit checks, or headless Chromium testing. Subjective fine-tuning of `pixelsToBoundary` (`210`) or `maxScreenOffsetX/Y` (`0.25` / `0.26`) can be adjusted in one place via `VIRTUAL_AIM_CONFIG` if you want an even tighter or wider envelope after live playtesting on your hardware mouse/DPI."
