  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Dynamic Controls**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `CameraController.ts` file. I\'ve realized the existing clamping on `lagX` and `lagY` to specific ranges, namely `[-1.65, 1.65]` and `[-1.15, 1.15]`, will keep fast turns dynamic while keeping the ship on screen. The architecture is clean, and the implications for control feel are significant!\n\n\n**Refining Steering Parameters**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications for game settings, and I am going to make it work cleanly across just four files. I\'m focusing on those files: `/src/types/game.ts`, `FlightController.ts`, `CameraController.ts` and `FlightHUD.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m integrating progressive mouse steering settings into `GameSettings`, including sensitivity multipliers and acceleration distances, aiming to create a nuanced control scheme. I\'m carefully considering how these new settings will interact with existing clamping mechanisms in `FlightController.ts` and UI elements in `FlightHUD.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Steering Controls**\n\nI\'m making good progress! I\'ve incorporated `responseCurve`, and `aimBoundarySize` into the system, with clean defaults and clamping in `ships.ts`. I am adding telemetry fields to `FlightTelemetry` for improved feedback and debugging. These fields, including `steeringZone`, `steeringSensitivityX`, `steeringSensitivityY`, and `steeringAccelRatio` will be useful! I\'m now working on the telemetry structure. I will integrate `PROGRESSIVE_STEERING_CONFIG` with defaults and helpers in `FlightController.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Sensitivity Equations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the mathematical underpinnings of the progressive steering. I\'ve been working on this pure function: `evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity`. I\'m using parameters like deadzone, boundary blend, and recovery smoothing to calculate target sensitivity. I need to make sure this can be used in both the runtime and unit tests with the exact same equation. I\'m adding `PROGRESSIVE_STEERING_CONFIG` defaults and helpers in `FlightController.ts`.\n\n\n**Calculating Sensitivity Targets**\n\nI\'ve worked out the progressive sensitivity calculation! If the absolute displacement is greater than the aim boundary, I calculate excess with `e = (absDisplacement - B) / S`, and use the curve factor to get target sensitivity. Now I can apply this equation in a loop per-axis inside `FlightController.update`, and the sensitivity of the X and Y axes look good. I\'ll test with the equations.\n\n\n**Defining Aim Boundaries**\n\nI am now focusing on aim boundary calculations. I\'m setting `B_y` as `B_x * 0.92` to match screen proportions. I\'m using `settings.accelerationDistance` for `S` and calculating `maxDispX` and `maxDispY`. I\'m accumulating relative mouse displacement, using `mouseSensitivity` and `invertY` in the calculations, and clamping `virtualAimX` and `virtualAimY`. I will call `evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity` independently for X and Y and integrate delta-time recovery smoothing.\n\n\n**Integrating Steering Commands**\n\nI\'m now integrating the sensitivity calculations to generate normalized steering commands per axis. I\'m computing `absNorm`, and if it exceeds the deadzone, I compute `u` and `baseSteer`. Finally, I\'m integrating the smoothed sensitivities to get `steerX` and `steerY`. I\'m repeating this for the Y axis, applying appropriate boundaries. These calculations are crucial for the responsiveness of the ship controls.\n\n\n\n**Refining Control Implementation**\n\nI\'m now integrating new calculations into my control scheme. I\'ve refined angular smoothing and am calculating the normalized steering commands per axis. I\'m focusing on reticle mapping, now. The virtual reticle movement within and outside the precision zone is crucial for the player\'s visual feedback. I\'m working on the logic for `aimCursorX/Y` and `aimScreenX/Y`, ensuring a smooth visual transition.\n\n\n**Visualizing Steering Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating visual cues for the progressive steering. In `FlightHUD.tsx`, I\'m dynamically updating the aiming boundary box based on `settings.aimBoundarySize`, giving it a nice visual design and applying subtle rounded corners. The border color and opacity, as well as the virtual cursor tint, will now respond to `t.steeringZone`, transitioning smoothly between cyan, amber-cyan, and cyan-white based on the steering state. In `SettingsPanel.tsx`, I\'m creating a new section to expose all six progressive mouse steering controls for configuration.\n\n\n**Defining Settings Configuration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the progressive mouse steering controls into the game settings. I\'m focusing on defining clear and concise parameters: base, boundary, and maximum sensitivities, acceleration distance, response curve, and aim boundary size. I\'ll make these accessible in both main and pause menu settings, with live updates and automatic persistence in `localStorage`. I\'m going to create a live SVG preview to show the response curve for player understanding.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "ax3_ap7CLdSv_PUPvZG3kQs"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_18264336336118967079"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add progressive mouse steering settings to GameSettings and steering zone telemetry to FlightTelemetry\", \"EndLine\":152, \"Instruction\":\"Add progressive mouse steering fields to GameSettings and FlightTelemetry in src/types/game.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export type SteeringZone = \'precision\' | \'transition\' | \'acceleration\';\\n\\nexport interface GameSettings {\\n  /** Base Sensitivity multiplier for relative mouse movement (0.3 to 2.5) */\\n  mouseSensitivity: number;\\n  /** Sensitivity multiplier immediately upon crossing the aiming boundary (0.15 to 1.0) */\\n  boundarySensitivity: number;\\n  /** Asymptotic maximum sensitivity multiplier in the acceleration zone (1.2 to 3.5) */\\n  maxSensitivity: number;\\n  /** Distance scale S (in virtual px) over which acceleration ramps outside the boundary (80 to 500) */\\n  accelerationDistance: number;\\n  /** Nonlinear response curve exponent p in f(e) = e^p / (1 + e^p) (1.0 to 3.5) */\\n  responseCurve: number;\\n  /** Half-width screen fraction of the precision aiming boundary (0.15 to 0.38) */\\n  aimBoundarySize: number;\\n  invertY: boolean;\\n  cameraDistance: number; // 7.2 to 13.5\\n  cameraSensitivity: number; // 0.6 to 1.6\\n  masterVolume: number; // 0 to 1\\n  graphicsQuality: GraphicsQuality;\\n  resolutionScale: number; // 0.65 to 1.0\\n  shadowQuality: ShadowQuality;\\n  particleQuality: EffectQuality;\\n  environmentDetail: EffectQuality;\\n  drawDistance: number; // 2000 to 5200\\n  antialias: boolean;\\n  postGlowEnabled: boolean;\\n  /** Development-only performance monitor toggle (hidden in production builds) */\\n  showPerfOverlay: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * High-frequency mutable telemetry updated every simulation frame.\\n * Read directly via refs inside HUD animation loops to guarantee zero React re-renders per frame.\\n */\\nexport interface FlightTelemetry {\\n  speed: number;\\n  signedSpeed: number;\\n  maxSpeed: number;\\n  effectiveMaxSpeed: number;\\n  throttle: number; // -1 to 1\\n  boostEnergy: number; // 0 to 100\\n  maxBoostEnergy: number;\\n  isBoosting: boolean;\\n  boostDepleted: boolean;\\n  boostIntensity: number; // 0 to 1 smoothly damped\\n  hull: number;\\n  maxHull: number;\\n  yawRate: number; // normalized angular velocity relative to base yawSpeed\\n  pitchRate: number; // normalized angular velocity relative to base pitchSpeed\\n  rollRate: number; // normalized -1..1\\n  /** Normalized virtual aim offset (-1..1 inside precision boundary) */\\n  aimNormalizedX: number;\\n  aimNormalizedY: number;\\n  /** Screen-space [0..1] position of virtual mouse steering reticle */\\n  aimScreenX: number;\\n  aimScreenY: number;\\n  /** Screen-space [0..1] position of ship boresight */\\n  boresightScreenX: number;\\n  boresightScreenY: number;\\n  /** Active progressive steering zone & smoothed per-axis sensitivity multipliers */\\n  steeringZone: SteeringZone;\\n  steeringSensitivityX: number;\\n  steeringSensitivityY: number;\\n  steeringAccelRatio: number; // 0..1 overdrive intensity beyond boundary\\n  headingDeg: number; // 0..359\\n  pitchDeg: number; // -90..90\\n  rollDeg: number; // -180..180\\n  altitude: number;\\n  status: FlightStatus;\\n  pointerLocked: boolean;\", \"StartLine\":96, \"TargetContent\":\"export interface GameSettings {\\n  mouseSensitivity: number; // 0.3 to 2.4\\n  invertY: boolean;\\n  cameraDistance: number; // 7.2 to 13.5\\n  cameraSensitivity: number; // 0.6 to 1.6\\n  masterVolume: number; // 0 to 1\\n  graphicsQuality: GraphicsQuality;\\n  resolutionScale: number; // 0.65 to 1.0\\n  shadowQuality: ShadowQuality;\\n  particleQuality: EffectQuality;\\n  environmentDetail: EffectQuality;\\n  drawDistance: number; // 2000 to 5200\\n  antialias: boolean;\\n  postGlowEnabled: boolean;\\n  /** Development-only performance monitor toggle (hidden in production builds) */\\n  showPerfOverlay: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * High-frequency mutable telemetry updated every simulation frame.\\n * Read directly via refs inside HUD animation loops to guarantee zero React re-renders per frame.\\n */\\nexport interface FlightTelemetry {\\n  speed: number;\\n  signedSpeed: number;\\n  maxSpeed: number;\\n  effectiveMaxSpeed: number;\\n  throttle: number; // -1 to 1\\n  boostEnergy: number; // 0 to 100\\n  maxBoostEnergy: number;\\n  isBoosting: boolean;\\n  boostDepleted: boolean;\\n  boostIntensity: number; // 0 to 1 smoothly damped\\n  hull: number;\\n  maxHull: number;\\n  yawRate: number; // normalized -1..1\\n  pitchRate: number; // normalized -1..1\\n  rollRate: number; // normalized -1..1\\n  /** Normalized instantaneous turn input feedback (-1..1) */\\n  aimNormalizedX: number;\\n  aimNormalizedY: number;\\n  /** Screen-space [0..1] position of true 3D weapon aiming reticle */\\n  aimScreenX: number;\\n  aimScreenY: number;\\n  /** Screen-space [0..1] position of ship boresight */\\n  boresightScreenX: number;\\n  boresightScreenY: number;\\n  headingDeg: number; // 0..359\\n  pitchDeg: number; // -90..90\\n  rollDeg: number; // -180..180\\n  altitude: number;\\n  status: FlightStatus;\\n  pointerLocked: boolean;\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/game.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating GameSettings and FlightTelemetry types\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update game types for progressive steering\"}"
