    thinking: "**Analyzing Test Output**\n\nI\'m incredibly relieved! The live browser test just revealed a critical oversight. Specifically, Step 4 in the output is crucial. Before that, steps A and B look good. The SETTINGS_UI looks present: all six sliders and the curve SVG are verified!\n\n\n**Examining Sensitivity Data**\n\nI\'ve been reviewing the latest data from the input manager. It seems that dispatchRel(-560, -80) was filtered out at the end, which is a key update. Prior to that, I\'ve got detailed readings. The data starts with initialization values and progresses through the precision and transition zones, then acceleration. Notably, the Y-axis sensitivity remains consistent while the X-axis sensitivity shows a clear evolution, reaching 2.054 at acceleration\'s deepest level!\n\n\n**Refining Usability Verification**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a real-world gameplay improvement. Because of the warp-spike guard, the initial `-560px` jump was filtered out. I need to verify that returning to Precision with realistic, multi-event mouse movements works smoothly and recovers `sensX` as expected, with updates to Settings UI. So, I will verify Step 4 with realistic events, and adjust `aimBoundarySize` in live Pause Settings to prove this is functioning as it should.\n\n\n"
