  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. Mathematical Response Curve & Steering Architecture\n\nProgressive mouse steering is evaluated **independently on the horizontal (yaw) and vertical (pitch) axes** from accumulated Pointer Lock relative displacement (`movementX`, `movementY`) with zero auto-recentering and zero dependence on absolute cursor coordinates.\n\nFor a single axis with accumulated displacement $x$ (scaled by **Base Sensitivity**), normal aiming boundary $B$, acceleration distance scale $S$, boundary sensitivity $s_B$, maximum sensitivity $s_{\\max}$, and response exponent $p$:\n\n1. **Precision Zone ($|x| \\le B$)**:\n   - Core region ($|x| \\le 0.80B$): exact normal sensitivity, $\\text{targetSens} = 1.0$.\n   - Boundary approach ($0.80B < |x| \\le B$): $C^1$-smooth cubic Hermite blend (`smoothstep`, $t^2(3 - 2t)$) from $1.0$ down to $s_B$ so both value and derivative match at $|x| = B$ with zero step discontinuity.\n2. **Transition & Acceleration Zones ($|x| > B$)**:\n   $$e = \\max\\!\\left(0,\\; \\frac{|x| - B}{S}\\right), \\qquad f(e) = \\frac{e^p}{1 + e^p}$$\n   $$\\text{targetSens}(e) = s_B + (s_{\\max} - s_B)\\,f(e)$$\n   - **Transition Zone** ($\\text{targetSens}(e) < 1.0$): immediately slower upon crossing $B$, climbing progressively as outward movement continues.\n   - **Acceleration Zone** ($\\text{targetSens}(e) \\ge 1.0$): smooth asymptotic turn speedup approaching $s_{\\max}$ without a hard steering cutoff, bounded by a safe per-axis angular rate ceiling (`3.2\303\227` yaw, `3.0\303\227` pitch) to prevent uncontrollable spin.\n3. **Delta-Time Recovery Smoothing**:\n   - Each axis filters $\\text{targetSens}$ independently via an exponential filter with time constant $\\tau = 0.12\\text{ s}$:\n     $$\\alpha = 1 - e^{-\\Delta t / 0.12}$$\n   - Eliminates sudden rotation spikes on rapid flicks across $B$ and produces a smooth return to precision steering.\n4. **Visual Reticle & Camera Separation**:\n   - Inside $|x| \\le B$, the virtual reticle tracks inside the configurable aiming boundary frame (`aimBoundarySize`). Beyond $B$, it anchors cleanly on the boundary edge with a subtle elastic stretch (`\342\211\244 2.8%` viewport) and subtle zone tinting (cyan \342\206\222 amber-cyan \342\206\222 energized cyan-white), never reaching screen corners or HUD panels.\n   - `CameraController` remains decoupled from mouse input and continues following ship orientation/velocity with existing Phase 1 damping and clamped turn lag.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Final Tuning Values & Player Settings\n\nAll six parameters are exposed in the **Settings** menu (accessible from both the Main Menu and Pause Menu), include a live SVG curve preview, apply immediately, and persist in `localStorage`:\n\n| Setting | Default | Range | Role |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **Base Sensitivity** | `1.00x` | `0.30x \342\200\223 2.50x` | Scales relative `movementX` / `movementY` accumulation |\n| **Boundary Sensitivity** | `0.35x` | `0.15x \342\200\223 1.00x` | Initial sensitivity right at/past the aiming boundary ($e = 0$) |\n| **Maximum Sensitivity** | `2.50x` | `1.20x \342\200\223 3.50x` | Asymptotic upper sensitivity multiplier in Acceleration Zone |\n| **Acceleration Distance** ($S$) | `240 px` | `80 \342\200\223 500 px` | Distance past $B$ where $f(1) = 0.50$ (halfway from $s_B$ to $s_{\\max}$) |\n| **Response Curve** ($p$) | `2.0` | `1.0 \342\200\223 3.5` | Nonlinearity exponent in $f(e) = e^p / (1 + e^p)$ |\n| **Aim Boundary Size** | `25%` (`0.25`) | `15% \342\200\223 38%` | Precision boundary half-width on screen & $B = 800 \\times \\text{size}$ (`200 px` default; vertical $B_y = 0.92 B_x$) |\n\nAdditional internal constants: center deadzone `0.03`, inner precision shaping exponent `1.15`, boundary blend start `0.80B`, recovery smoothing `0.12s`, and upper displacement buffer `4.0 \303\227 S` past $B$ (at $e = 4.0$, $f(4) = 0.941$).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Verification Results\n\n#### Build & Static Analysis\n- **Build (`compile_applet`)**: Succeeded.\n- **TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`)**: Passed with 0 errors.\n\n#### Simulation & Frame-Rate Stability (`tsx`)\n- **Curve & settled yaw rates** (Interceptor, default settings, `B = 200 px`, `S = 240 px`, `p = 2.0`):\n  - Precision (`140 px`): `sens = 1.000x`, `1.372 rad/s`\n  - Transition (`215 px`, just past boundary): `sens = 0.359x`, `0.757 rad/s` (visibly slower)\n  - Transition rising (`300 px`): `sens = 0.669x`, `1.405 rad/s`\n  - Acceleration (`440 px`, $e = 1.0$): `sens = 1.424x`, `2.990 rad/s`\n  - Deep Acceleration (`680 px`, $e = 2.0$): `sens = 2.068x`, `4.340 rad/s`\n- **No sudden rotation spikes**: Across a continuous `0 \342\206\222 750 px` sweep at 60 Hz, maximum single-frame yaw velocity delta was `0.158 rad/s`.\n- **Frame-rate consistency** (`1.0s` hold across `30 / 60 / 120 / 240 Hz`):\n  - Precision (`120 px`): `-62.13\302\260 / -61.66\302\260 / -61.41\302\260 / -61.27\302\260` (`< 0.9\302\260` spread)\n  - Transition (`220 px`): `-49.73\302\260 / -50.00\302\260 / -50.14\302\260 / -50.21\302\260` (`< 0.5\302\260` spread)\n  - Acceleration (`440 px`): `-157.86\302\260 / -156.22\302\260 / -155.35\302\260 / -154.90\302\260` (identical settled `sensX = 1.425x`)\n\n#### Live Browser Verification (Headless Chromium, `1280\303\227720`, Mission M-01)\n- **Settings UI**: Confirmed all 6 sliders and live SVG curve preview render cleanly; changing **Aim Boundary Size** (`0.25 \342\206\222 0.32`) from Pause Settings persisted to `localStorage` and resized the live HUD boundary frame from `640 px` to `819 px` (exact `0.32 \303\227 2 \303\227 1280`).\n- **Pointer Lock & Edge Continuity**: Owned by `CANVAS`, `0` `pointerlockerror` events, `0` page/console errors, `0.0 px` rollback while held stationary at boundaries.\n- **Three Zones Live**:\n  - **Precision (`+140 px`)**: `zone = precision`, `cursorX = 864.0`, `sensX = 1.000`, `\316\224HDG = +22\302\260` over 4 frames.\n  - **Transition (`+220 px`)**: `zone = transition`, `cursorX = 960.2`, `sensX = 0.375`, `\316\224HDG = +10\302\260` over 4 frames (slower immediately past boundary).\n  - **Acceleration (`+440 px`, $e = 1.0$)**: `zone = acceleration`, `cursorX = 977.9`, `sensX = 1.400`, `\316\224HDG = +32\302\260` over 4 frames.\n  - **Deep Acceleration + Independent Y (`+680 px X`, `+80 px Y`)**: `zone = acceleration`, `cursorX = 988.7`, `cursorY = 441.4`, `sensX = 2.054`, `sensY = 1.000` (vertical axis unaffected), `\316\224HDG = +49\302\260` over 4 frames.\n- **Smooth Return to Precision (`+680 px \342\206\222 +120 px` via realistic `-70 px` events)**: Returned immediately to `zone = precision` (`cursorX = 832.0`) while `sensX` smoothly decayed `2.061 \342\206\222 1.700 \342\206\222 1.200 \342\206\222 1.025 \342\206\222 1.000` with zero snap.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Remaining Issues\n\n- No functional defects or regressions were observed in simulation or live browser tests.\n- Returning from deep acceleration (`e = 2.0\342\200\2234.0`) currently tracks mouse displacement symmetrically `1:1`; if after hands-on playtesting on your mouse DPI you want an even faster physical pull-back from deep acceleration into precision, an optional inward-return multiplier can be added without altering stationary boundary hold behavior."
    message_id: "oB__arLqGvH5-8YPqu_C8Qg"
